1
00:00:02,117 --> 00:00:04,257
(One Summer Day)

2
00:00:04,257 --> 00:00:06,327
- Nice to see you. - Nice to see you all.

3
00:00:06,327 --> 00:00:08,827
It's time to bring in the star of this week's Rainbow Live.

4
00:00:08,827 --> 00:00:10,897
I've never had the chance to meet her in person.

5
00:00:10,897 --> 00:00:12,167
But Kim Sook...

6
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:14,467
has been telling me about her for about six months.

7
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:16,707
- Really? - Sook said she was an amazing girl.

8
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:18,574
Sook said we had to invite her.

9
00:00:18,574 --> 00:00:20,474
- I see. - So I strongly recommended her too.

10
00:00:20,474 --> 00:00:23,044
She captured the hearts of many great actors and actresses.

11
00:00:23,074 --> 00:00:25,074
- Her acting is superb. - Right.

12
00:00:25,074 --> 00:00:27,544
It's Actress Ryu Hye Young.

13
00:00:27,544 --> 00:00:28,814
- Welcome. - Oh, my.

14
00:00:28,814 --> 00:00:30,014
I'm finally meeting her in person.

15
00:00:30,014 --> 00:00:31,284
- We're meeting her in person. - That's right.

16
00:00:31,284 --> 00:00:32,284
Oh, my.

17
00:00:32,284 --> 00:00:33,954
- Hello. - Hello.

18
00:00:35,068 --> 00:00:37,008
(She left a strong impression on the viewers...)

19
00:00:37,008 --> 00:00:39,478
(as the grumpy, but intelligent girl in "Reply 1988.")

20
00:00:39,478 --> 00:00:40,508
Hey. Here's the thing.

21
00:00:40,508 --> 00:00:42,878
(She perfectly pulled off all of her characters.)

22
00:00:44,678 --> 00:00:46,518
(Always the scene-stealer...)

23
00:00:46,518 --> 00:00:49,088
(who caught the viewers' attention regardless of her roles)

24
00:00:49,718 --> 00:00:52,488
Hello. I've been living alone for 11 years.

25
00:00:52,488 --> 00:00:54,018
I'm Actress Ryu Hye Young.

26
00:00:54,188 --> 00:00:55,288
Eleven years?

27
00:00:55,828 --> 00:00:57,328
(Welcome to the show.)

28
00:00:57,328 --> 00:00:58,898
- This is your first time here. - Yes.

29
00:00:58,998 --> 00:01:00,658
Could you tell us how it feels to be here?

30
00:01:00,658 --> 00:01:04,098
Well, the studio is smaller than I expected.

31
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:08,338
It makes me feel cozy that I could talk more comfortably here.

32
00:01:08,338 --> 00:01:09,438
- Actually, - I'm looking forward to it.

33
00:01:09,608 --> 00:01:11,808
- before you arrived, - Yes.

34
00:01:11,908 --> 00:01:13,178
Sung Hwan said...

35
00:01:13,178 --> 00:01:15,478
- he was a huge fan. - Well...

36
00:01:15,478 --> 00:01:16,778
- Really? - Yes.

37
00:01:16,778 --> 00:01:19,578
I saw you in the short film and the independent film as well.

38
00:01:19,578 --> 00:01:20,918
My voice is shaking.

39
00:01:20,918 --> 00:01:22,948
I've been a huge fan for a long time.

40
00:01:23,148 --> 00:01:24,148
Thank you.

41
00:01:24,448 --> 00:01:25,588
Where are you looking at?

42
00:01:25,588 --> 00:01:26,888
People might think you're my fan.

43
00:01:27,188 --> 00:01:29,588
It's my first time meeting Hye Young in person too.

44
00:01:29,588 --> 00:01:31,828
I didn't know you were this stylish.

45
00:01:31,828 --> 00:01:33,428
I had no idea you had such a cool vibe.

46
00:01:33,428 --> 00:01:35,228
She's famous among fashion enthusiasts.

47
00:01:35,228 --> 00:01:37,128
- Really? - Yes.

48
00:01:37,128 --> 00:01:38,828
- She's very fashionable. - She is...

49
00:01:39,738 --> 00:01:41,368
Did you cut your own hair?

50
00:01:41,738 --> 00:01:43,738
I didn't cut it myself.

51
00:01:43,738 --> 00:01:45,578
But I did tell them how I wanted it to be cut.

52
00:01:45,578 --> 00:01:46,578
- They took your feedback. - Yes.

53
00:01:46,578 --> 00:01:48,108
- You have a wild hairstyle. - Are you crazy?

54
00:01:48,508 --> 00:01:49,748
I like wild vibes.

55
00:01:49,748 --> 00:01:51,578
All right. Let's check out her clips together.

56
00:01:53,018 --> 00:01:54,278
(A Weird Adult)

57
00:01:54,278 --> 00:01:55,448
"A weird adult?"

58
00:01:56,788 --> 00:01:59,218
(It's quiet and dark in the room.)

59
00:01:59,218 --> 00:02:00,988
- You have the blackout curtains. - Yes.

60
00:02:01,588 --> 00:02:03,058
I wake up...

61
00:02:03,328 --> 00:02:05,998
immediately when there's even a tiny bit of sunlight.

62
00:02:05,998 --> 00:02:07,028
- You're a light sleeper. - I love those curtains.

63
00:02:07,028 --> 00:02:08,728
My room has to be completely dark like yours.

64
00:02:15,038 --> 00:02:18,038
(Tossing and turning)

65
00:02:19,578 --> 00:02:22,578
(She turns on her tablet PC, not the light at 11:13am.)

66
00:02:24,408 --> 00:02:25,878
(Yawning)

67
00:02:31,588 --> 00:02:32,958
- Everyone... - She's watching YouTube.

68
00:02:32,958 --> 00:02:34,918
- As soon as you wake up? - Yes. It's fixed.

69
00:02:34,918 --> 00:02:36,758
- I see. I know what it is. - It must be the holder.

70
00:02:36,758 --> 00:02:37,858
- It's the holder. - It is.

71
00:02:38,128 --> 00:02:40,428
(Wide awake)

72
00:02:41,358 --> 00:02:42,468
Hello.

73
00:02:42,928 --> 00:02:46,138
I've been living alone for 11 years now.

74
00:02:46,538 --> 00:02:48,038
I'm Actress Ryu Hye Young.

75
00:02:50,168 --> 00:02:53,108
(Hye Young starts her day by watching a video.)

76
00:02:54,178 --> 00:02:55,478
(Sluggish)

77
00:02:56,808 --> 00:02:58,408
(She's on her phone.)

78
00:02:58,408 --> 00:03:00,078
(Ringing)

79
00:03:00,948 --> 00:03:02,718
Have you traveled abroad recently?

80
00:03:03,418 --> 00:03:04,548
- What? - Did something break down?

81
00:03:05,658 --> 00:03:08,658
It's been ages since I traveled abroad.

82
00:03:10,728 --> 00:03:12,028
- It's an app. - An app?

83
00:03:12,028 --> 00:03:13,028
It helps me study.

84
00:03:13,028 --> 00:03:14,558
Is it Duolingo?

85
00:03:14,798 --> 00:03:17,298
- I'm on Duolingo and Speak. - I see. You use Speak.

86
00:03:18,498 --> 00:03:20,298
When did you start learning English?

87
00:03:20,598 --> 00:03:23,468
It's been two years...

88
00:03:24,208 --> 00:03:25,678
since I...

89
00:03:26,538 --> 00:03:27,538
No.

90
00:03:27,878 --> 00:03:31,208
I've been learning English for two years.

91
00:03:32,048 --> 00:03:33,518
(Ding)

92
00:03:35,218 --> 00:03:37,018
(She studies Japanese after English.)

93
00:03:37,018 --> 00:03:38,148
- What? - Japanese?

94
00:03:38,148 --> 00:03:39,418
You're also studying Japanese.

95
00:03:39,758 --> 00:03:41,758
- You start the next one right away. - I start it right away.

96
00:03:42,088 --> 00:03:43,188
I'm on the next app.

97
00:03:43,488 --> 00:03:44,828
- As soon as you wake up? - Two languages?

98
00:03:46,458 --> 00:03:50,498
(Focused on learning languages while lying on her bed)

99
00:03:51,828 --> 00:03:54,968
I wanted to do at least one thing a day...

100
00:03:55,198 --> 00:04:00,008
that I could compliment myself for.

101
00:04:00,238 --> 00:04:04,248
Maybe, I wanted to feel a sense of achievement...

102
00:04:04,778 --> 00:04:06,578
from doing something small like that.

103
00:04:06,648 --> 00:04:07,878
(Smiling)

104
00:04:08,118 --> 00:04:10,018
- Once you feel it, - Right.

105
00:04:10,018 --> 00:04:11,018
- you get addicted to that feeling. - It's an...

106
00:04:11,018 --> 00:04:12,418
- addiction indeed. - Right.

107
00:04:13,688 --> 00:04:17,188
(She hasn't budged an inch on her bed after waking up.)

108
00:04:17,858 --> 00:04:21,028
(She kept studying for about an hour.)

109
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:22,868
She might spend her entire day on her bed.

110
00:04:22,868 --> 00:04:24,498
(She's studying hard in her dark room.)

111
00:04:25,668 --> 00:04:26,868
Why is this so hard?

112
00:04:27,238 --> 00:04:29,508
(On a 196-day streak)

113
00:04:29,508 --> 00:04:31,468
I've been studying for 196 consecutive days.

114
00:04:31,568 --> 00:04:32,878
- For 196 days? - Yes.

115
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:35,008
- It's been 196 days so far. - You're very persistent.

116
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:36,308
It's not easy to collect the flame stickers.

117
00:04:37,078 --> 00:04:39,178
(Getting up)

118
00:04:39,578 --> 00:04:41,378
You came up with a really nice daily routine.

119
00:04:41,378 --> 00:04:43,048
- She didn't go back to sleep. - She really keeps this up.

120
00:04:43,048 --> 00:04:45,218
Right. I can see that she does this every day.

121
00:04:45,418 --> 00:04:46,688
She's very diligent.

122
00:04:47,658 --> 00:04:50,988
(She gets out of her bed after studying languages.)

123
00:04:50,988 --> 00:04:52,858
(Tossing)

124
00:04:55,898 --> 00:04:57,628
(Hye Young leaves her dark bedroom at last.)

125
00:04:57,628 --> 00:04:58,698
No.

126
00:05:02,168 --> 00:05:03,168
All right.

127
00:05:07,538 --> 00:05:09,348
My gosh. You don't have any sunlight in your house.

128
00:05:09,878 --> 00:05:12,248
They are also blackout curtains.

129
00:05:12,248 --> 00:05:13,318
My gosh.

130
00:05:14,348 --> 00:05:17,218
(She moves around in the dark.)

131
00:05:20,158 --> 00:05:23,558
I've been living in this house for a year and a half now.

132
00:05:26,028 --> 00:05:28,058
I renovated the house a bit.

133
00:05:28,128 --> 00:05:32,398
I decorated the house to suit my style.

134
00:05:32,598 --> 00:05:33,968
It's my cozy little house.

135
00:05:33,968 --> 00:05:35,938
- Your house has a simple look. - Yes.

136
00:05:36,568 --> 00:05:41,078
This house has white floors and wooden molding.

137
00:05:41,078 --> 00:05:43,248
- My gosh. - I wanted some decorative props.

138
00:05:43,648 --> 00:05:45,578
Colorful decor...

139
00:05:45,578 --> 00:05:48,918
looked pretty good in this house.

140
00:05:49,588 --> 00:05:52,148
- What a cute place. - It's got a minimalistic charm too.

141
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:53,888
You must like toy figurines.

142
00:05:54,118 --> 00:05:55,688
I can never say no to cute things.

143
00:05:55,858 --> 00:05:57,258
- They're so cute. - They're hard to say no to.

144
00:05:57,828 --> 00:06:01,658
This is a very old apartment.

145
00:06:02,158 --> 00:06:04,568
So I started to bring in more colors to this house.

146
00:06:05,598 --> 00:06:07,868
This house bears the marks of time.

147
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:09,668
- That's how it used to look before? - Yes.

148
00:06:09,868 --> 00:06:12,778
I kept the renovation to the minimum.

149
00:06:13,478 --> 00:06:14,608
It looks like a brand-new house.

150
00:06:16,148 --> 00:06:18,508
(An old-fashioned kitchen)

151
00:06:19,778 --> 00:06:21,718
- Wait, you did it yourself? - Yes, I did.

152
00:06:24,088 --> 00:06:25,218
(She replaced it with a clean stainless table.)

153
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:28,318
- Gosh. That will stay clean. - She has an eye for this.

154
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:32,158
I measured the size and custom-ordered the plate.

155
00:06:32,358 --> 00:06:33,728
- Did she put it over? - I placed it over the table.

156
00:06:33,858 --> 00:06:35,758
- You did? - Yes, I could do that.

157
00:06:35,758 --> 00:06:36,798
Right.

158
00:06:37,228 --> 00:06:39,568
Stainless steel, wood, and white...

159
00:06:39,868 --> 00:06:41,538
were the core themes.

160
00:06:41,898 --> 00:06:45,438
I kept the decoration work to the minimum.

161
00:06:45,638 --> 00:06:46,678
How neat.

162
00:06:47,308 --> 00:06:49,578
- The house suits you. - Right.

163
00:06:49,578 --> 00:06:52,178
- Really? Thank you. - The house suits your image.

164
00:06:54,078 --> 00:06:55,918
(Walking over)

165
00:06:55,918 --> 00:06:57,088
Get some sunlight.

166
00:06:58,048 --> 00:06:59,858
(She opens the curtain just slightly.)

167
00:06:59,858 --> 00:07:01,118
Get some sunlight.

168
00:07:03,758 --> 00:07:05,188
- My gosh. - What?

169
00:07:05,188 --> 00:07:07,098
- Do you have a cat? - What's going on?

170
00:07:09,398 --> 00:07:11,298
- Why did you stop growing? - What?

171
00:07:13,468 --> 00:07:16,008
(It's Hye Young's plant.)

172
00:07:16,008 --> 00:07:17,308
- You have a plant. - Yes.

173
00:07:17,538 --> 00:07:20,078
How beautiful. Get some sunlight. Only you should get the sunlight.

174
00:07:20,278 --> 00:07:22,038
(A tiny gap)

175
00:07:22,678 --> 00:07:24,848
(She timidly opens it a little more.)

176
00:07:26,018 --> 00:07:27,118
You drew them just enough...

177
00:07:27,118 --> 00:07:28,218
- for the plant to get sunlight. - Yes.

178
00:07:28,218 --> 00:07:30,148
I only let my plant get some sunlight.

179
00:07:30,788 --> 00:07:33,858
Is there a reason you don't want any sunlight in your house?

180
00:07:34,588 --> 00:07:37,958
It started when I was filming "Reply 1988."

181
00:07:37,958 --> 00:07:41,328
I suddenly got so much attention from the public.

182
00:07:41,928 --> 00:07:43,998
I realized that my words...

183
00:07:43,998 --> 00:07:46,538
- had power. - I see.

184
00:07:46,538 --> 00:07:47,868
That's when I realized it.

185
00:07:47,868 --> 00:07:50,608
That made me be more careful with my words.

186
00:07:50,768 --> 00:07:51,838
I got more timid...

187
00:07:51,838 --> 00:07:53,308
- at meeting people. - You got timid. I see.

188
00:07:53,878 --> 00:07:56,648
- I get scared easily. - Really?

189
00:07:56,648 --> 00:07:57,978
- You suddenly felt anxious. - Yes.

190
00:07:57,978 --> 00:08:01,818
I usually keep the curtains closed due to my anxiety too.

191
00:08:03,248 --> 00:08:05,118
(Only her plant is allowed to get sunlight.)

192
00:08:05,118 --> 00:08:07,388
Why did you stop growing? Do you want more water?

193
00:08:07,388 --> 00:08:08,418
(Why did you stop growing? Do you want more water?)

194
00:08:09,758 --> 00:08:11,558
- What are you doing? - You were growing.

195
00:08:11,558 --> 00:08:12,758
(She quickly checks for moisture with bare hands.)

196
00:08:13,828 --> 00:08:16,298
(I think you have enough water.)

197
00:08:17,498 --> 00:08:19,098
Why did you stop?

198
00:08:19,838 --> 00:08:21,538
Please answer me.

199
00:08:21,768 --> 00:08:23,268
Yes, I hear some people do this.

200
00:08:23,408 --> 00:08:25,638
They talk to their plant when they wake up.

201
00:08:25,638 --> 00:08:27,538
- You have to. - You have to do that.

202
00:08:27,538 --> 00:08:30,578
They're also alive. So they can understand everything.

203
00:08:31,478 --> 00:08:34,018
You can do this, right?

204
00:08:35,748 --> 00:08:37,848
I don't know much about plants.

205
00:08:38,148 --> 00:08:40,558
I asked my expert friends.

206
00:08:40,688 --> 00:08:44,688
I trimmed my plant. Afterward, it started to grow again.

207
00:08:45,028 --> 00:08:46,758
My plant needs some cheering.

208
00:08:48,558 --> 00:08:50,468
Only that one gets sunlight.

209
00:08:50,468 --> 00:08:51,798
- Yes. - I trimmed it.

210
00:08:51,968 --> 00:08:53,868
I say hello to my plant every day.

211
00:08:53,998 --> 00:08:55,038
I say goodnight to it...

212
00:08:55,038 --> 00:08:56,268
- before going to sleep. - Yes.

213
00:08:56,568 --> 00:08:58,338
"You can do this. We're in this together."

214
00:08:58,338 --> 00:09:00,738
"We're one."

215
00:09:00,738 --> 00:09:02,778
"If you die, I die too." I'd say things like that.

216
00:09:03,278 --> 00:09:07,078
This is the longest plant I've ever had without killing it.

217
00:09:07,078 --> 00:09:08,148
(More affectionate for her longest-surviving plant)

218
00:09:08,848 --> 00:09:10,318
How beautiful.

219
00:09:11,418 --> 00:09:13,358
(After checking up on her plant,)

220
00:09:13,358 --> 00:09:15,058
(she goes to the dressing room.)

221
00:09:15,758 --> 00:09:17,558
(Pulling)

222
00:09:18,728 --> 00:09:20,558
(Plopping down)

223
00:09:24,228 --> 00:09:25,328
They're toe socks.

224
00:09:25,768 --> 00:09:27,268
(Popping out)

225
00:09:27,598 --> 00:09:28,968
I started to wear...

226
00:09:28,968 --> 00:09:32,168
toe socks for my foot health.

227
00:09:32,168 --> 00:09:34,738
People said they were better for my feet, so I tried them on.

228
00:09:34,738 --> 00:09:36,278
And I liked them.

229
00:09:36,278 --> 00:09:38,678
- That's a good thing. - Toe socks are comfortable for me.

230
00:09:38,678 --> 00:09:40,118
- Are you wearing them today? - Actually, I'm wearing...

231
00:09:40,118 --> 00:09:41,418
- Toe socks. - toe socks.

232
00:09:41,418 --> 00:09:42,448
- You really are. - Toe socks

233
00:09:42,448 --> 00:09:44,718
- My gosh. - You really are. So cute.

234
00:09:45,148 --> 00:09:47,988
They look stylish because you're wearing them.

235
00:09:47,988 --> 00:09:49,858
- Hey, if... - Being able to...

236
00:09:49,858 --> 00:09:51,158
move our toes individually...

237
00:09:51,158 --> 00:09:53,828
is more beneficial to our foot health.

238
00:09:55,198 --> 00:09:56,898
(With her warm feet,)

239
00:09:56,898 --> 00:09:58,668
(she goes to the living room.)

240
00:10:01,838 --> 00:10:04,208
(She fixes her sitting posture.)

241
00:10:04,208 --> 00:10:05,638
(Focused)

242
00:10:06,838 --> 00:10:07,938
Oh, my.

243
00:10:10,408 --> 00:10:12,278
- What is it? - Will she play music?

244
00:10:13,048 --> 00:10:14,718
I can't predict what she'll do next.

245
00:10:18,218 --> 00:10:20,788
(She stares at something with intense focus.)

246
00:10:20,788 --> 00:10:21,888
No.

247
00:10:23,688 --> 00:10:24,858
- What is it? - It's 3.25 percent...

248
00:10:24,858 --> 00:10:26,398
lactose-free milk.

249
00:10:26,928 --> 00:10:30,198
I like watching housewives' vlog videos.

250
00:10:30,198 --> 00:10:34,838
A lot of their vlog videos show their daily lives.

251
00:10:34,838 --> 00:10:36,038
- Housewives' vlog videos? - Yes.

252
00:10:36,038 --> 00:10:37,238
They're super popular.

253
00:10:37,368 --> 00:10:41,108
Watching other people go on with their ordinary lives...

254
00:10:41,638 --> 00:10:44,348
gives me a huge sense of stability.

255
00:10:44,548 --> 00:10:46,218
I seek peacefulness...

256
00:10:46,448 --> 00:10:48,848
from ordinary day-to-day lives.

257
00:10:48,848 --> 00:10:50,148
That's how I am.

258
00:10:50,148 --> 00:10:52,218
- They give a sense of comfort. - Yes.

259
00:10:52,588 --> 00:10:56,588
So I keep watching housewives' vlog videos.

260
00:10:59,058 --> 00:11:00,558
I think she needs to hire a helper.

261
00:11:02,428 --> 00:11:03,828
That part is too weak.

262
00:11:03,828 --> 00:11:05,628
(She's completely in sync with the housewife.)

263
