As I wait four years, I wait for the next World Soccer Games.

1050
00:44:02,678 --> 00:44:05,008
To be honest, I've lived for this day.

1051
00:44:05,278 --> 00:44:09,018
North and Central America has a major time difference,

1052
00:44:09,378 --> 00:44:11,518
so I've adjusted my body for two months.

1053
00:44:11,518 --> 00:44:12,548
To watch the games?

1054
00:44:12,848 --> 00:44:16,018
- You act like you're playing. - That was why you woke up early.

1055
00:44:17,088 --> 00:44:21,388
(Shall I get ready to root for the team?)

1056
00:44:22,758 --> 00:44:24,058
His house is clean.

1057
00:44:26,428 --> 00:44:28,098
(Throwing)

1058
00:44:28,998 --> 00:44:30,338
How many uniforms are there?

1059
00:44:30,768 --> 00:44:31,908
Oh, my.

1060
00:44:33,638 --> 00:44:35,978
(Spreading)

1061
00:44:36,608 --> 00:44:37,708
Gue Sung.

1062
00:44:38,408 --> 00:44:40,208
- Our member. - That's his uniform.

1063
00:44:41,918 --> 00:44:43,018
Hee Chan.

1064
00:44:43,918 --> 00:44:46,318
I only got the uniforms of the world-class players.

1065
00:44:46,318 --> 00:44:47,348
- That's a gauge. - Yes.

1066
00:44:47,348 --> 00:44:48,818
- A gauge for world-class players. - A gauge for world-class players.

1067
00:44:49,818 --> 00:44:52,528
Gosh, this is it.

1068
00:44:53,758 --> 00:44:54,828
Lee Young Pyo.

1069
00:44:54,828 --> 00:44:56,328
- Young Pyo. He is my friend. - That's incredible.

1070
00:44:57,358 --> 00:45:00,828
Lee Young Pyo actually wore this uniform.

1071
00:45:01,098 --> 00:45:02,838
- Was that a match-worn jersey? - He actually wore it.

1072
00:45:02,838 --> 00:45:04,298
- Gosh, that's precious. - He actually wore it?

1073
00:45:04,298 --> 00:45:06,238
- How did you get that? - He gave it to me as a gift.

1074
00:45:06,308 --> 00:45:07,468
- Really? - He gave it to you himself?

1075
00:45:07,768 --> 00:45:08,808
What about me?

1076
00:45:08,908 --> 00:45:10,338
(Desperate)

1077
00:45:10,478 --> 00:45:12,348
We had an opportunity to meet.

1078
00:45:12,348 --> 00:45:14,348
We ate together.

1079
00:45:14,508 --> 00:45:17,648
He knew I was a soccer fan, so he prepared that for me.

1080
00:45:17,778 --> 00:45:19,288
- I'm jealous. - That's a family treasure.

1081
00:45:19,288 --> 00:45:20,548
- That's a family treasure. - That's a family treasure.

1082
00:45:21,318 --> 00:45:22,888
This is my treasure.

1083
00:45:25,128 --> 00:45:27,888
(He spreads out his other jerseys.)

1084
00:45:28,628 --> 00:45:30,458
(Impressed)

1085
00:45:31,328 --> 00:45:33,228
- Lee Young Pyo and Park Ji Sung. - Park Ji Sung!

1086
00:45:33,798 --> 00:45:35,168
That was remade recently.

1087
00:45:35,168 --> 00:45:37,468
- Right. It was remade. - It was remade.

1088
00:45:37,898 --> 00:45:39,268
Can you tell just by looking at that?

1089
00:45:39,268 --> 00:45:41,238
- Yes. - Yes. I can tell right away.

1090
00:45:41,238 --> 00:45:42,538
Gosh, number 21.

1091
00:45:42,608 --> 00:45:44,638
- It brings back memories. - Right.

1092
00:45:46,048 --> 00:45:47,708
(I must take a picture of this.)

1093
00:45:47,708 --> 00:45:48,778
Oh, yes!

1094
00:45:50,678 --> 00:45:53,288
- Oh, yes! - He looks so happy.

1095
00:45:53,288 --> 00:45:54,618
(Happy)

1096
00:45:56,218 --> 00:45:57,288
(I can't leave out the cheering items.)

1097
00:45:57,288 --> 00:45:58,558
- He has those prepared as well? - He's fully equipped.

1098
00:45:58,558 --> 00:46:02,528
That's the standard set for those who like soccer.

1099
00:46:02,528 --> 00:46:05,128
- It's the standard form. - I see.

1100
00:46:05,128 --> 00:46:07,628
(He transforms into a Red Devil instantly with the basic items.)

1101
00:46:09,198 --> 00:46:12,208
- The vuvuzela. - That one is for daily use.

1102
00:46:12,208 --> 00:46:13,568
(He checks the sound of the vuvuzela as well.)

1103
00:46:13,568 --> 00:46:14,938
I'll need this...

1104
00:46:15,508 --> 00:46:16,508
and this.

1105
00:46:16,508 --> 00:46:18,008
(He diligently packs various cheering items.)

1106
00:46:19,408 --> 00:46:20,478
On top of this,

1107
00:46:20,478 --> 00:46:22,478
(CODE KUNST is fully dressed in black.)

1108
00:46:23,618 --> 00:46:25,618
I'll wear this today.

1109
00:46:27,888 --> 00:46:29,488
(Fitting in)

1110
00:46:32,258 --> 00:46:33,688
(A jersey with CODE KUNST in the back)

1111
00:46:33,688 --> 00:46:34,828
It's "CODE KUNST!"

1112
00:46:34,828 --> 00:46:35,958
- Nice. - You have that?

1113
00:46:37,458 --> 00:46:38,568
(Checking here and there)

1114
00:46:38,568 --> 00:46:39,828
Okay!

1115
00:46:40,528 --> 00:46:42,138
I look like a soccer freak.

1116
00:46:42,138 --> 00:46:43,398
(Greatly satisfied)

1117
00:46:44,868 --> 00:46:46,108
(He quickly gets ready to leave...)

1118
00:46:46,108 --> 00:46:47,338
(after being satisfied with his look.)

1119
00:46:47,338 --> 00:46:49,178
- He's actually leaving. - He's actually leaving.

1120
00:46:49,178 --> 00:46:50,808
- Yes. - Are you watching the game outside?

1121
00:46:50,978 --> 00:46:53,848
That day, people watched the match on the streets of Gwanghwamun Gate.

1122
00:46:53,908 --> 00:46:55,348
- Right. - Many people came out.

1123
00:46:55,548 --> 00:46:56,918
Is he going out to the streets?

1124
00:46:57,048 --> 00:46:58,548
If he's fully equipped like that,

1125
00:46:58,548 --> 00:46:59,588
- Did he go to Gwanghwamun Gate? - he should go to Gwanghwamun Gate.

1126
00:46:59,588 --> 00:47:00,718
- Right. - Right.

1127
00:47:01,858 --> 00:47:02,858
All right.

1128
00:47:02,858 --> 00:47:04,688
(Do well to protect the house, Panda.)

1129
00:47:04,688 --> 00:47:06,588
(Have a good time.)

1130
00:47:07,588 --> 00:47:11,528
(Singing)

1131
00:47:11,528 --> 00:47:14,228
- Gosh. - Why am I stuck at that song?

1132
00:47:14,398 --> 00:47:15,498
Why didn't you sing "Kick It?"

1133
00:47:15,498 --> 00:47:18,038
(Released in 2002)

1134
00:47:19,368 --> 00:47:21,368
(While singing cheer songs of his memories,)

1135
00:47:21,368 --> 00:47:24,178
(he excitedly heads somewhere.)

1136
00:47:25,308 --> 00:47:28,648
(I will be with you)

1137
00:47:28,648 --> 00:47:30,648
This song speaks to me.

1138
00:47:30,678 --> 00:47:31,718
It's a nice song.

1139
00:47:31,818 --> 00:47:33,718
You feel a bit emotional as you sing it.

1140
00:47:33,718 --> 00:47:34,788
- Right. - Right.

1141
00:47:36,618 --> 00:47:37,688
(Hey!)

1142
00:47:37,958 --> 00:47:39,588
It should be done with the car horn.

1143
00:47:40,728 --> 00:47:42,528
That was how it was done.

1144
00:47:44,898 --> 00:47:46,968
- Is that 2002? - Gosh!

1145
00:47:46,968 --> 00:47:48,298
(Everyone in the country was a Red Devil.)

1146
00:47:48,298 --> 00:47:49,538
I did that as well.

1147
00:47:49,538 --> 00:47:51,398
I went on top of some guy's car.

1148
00:47:51,398 --> 00:47:54,068
Right. People went on top of buses.

1149
00:47:54,068 --> 00:47:55,878
Weren't you all kids in 2002?

1150
00:47:55,878 --> 00:47:57,138
I was in middle school.

1151
00:47:57,138 --> 00:47:58,478
- I was 20. - I was in elementary school.

1152
00:47:58,478 --> 00:47:59,608
- I was a high school senior. - I was in eighth grade.

1153
00:47:59,608 --> 00:48:00,878
- I was in college. - You were in eighth grade?

1154
00:48:00,878 --> 00:48:02,178
- I was in eighth grade. - I was in middle school.

1155
00:48:02,378 --> 00:48:04,448
(You were in 8th grade in 2002?)

1156
00:48:04,548 --> 00:48:05,788
- How old are you? - Where did you watch the games?

1157
00:48:05,788 --> 00:48:06,948
- I was born in 1988. - What?

1158
00:48:08,488 --> 00:48:09,758
That's amazing.

1159
00:48:10,058 --> 00:48:11,988
- Where did you watch the games? - I was born in 1988.

1160
00:48:12,558 --> 00:48:14,888
I actually watched the game in Incheon.

1161
00:48:14,888 --> 00:48:16,498
- You actually watched it? - The match against Portugal...

1162
00:48:16,498 --> 00:48:17,528
when Park Ji Sung scored.

1163
00:48:17,828 --> 00:48:19,298
- I was there. - The Munhak Stadium?

1164
00:48:19,298 --> 00:48:20,868
- Right. I watched it there. - Really?

1165
00:48:22,568 --> 00:48:25,138
(He witnessed the historical moment.)

1166
00:48:25,968 --> 00:48:28,808
(Living witness of history, young Hyun Moo)

1167
00:48:28,938 --> 00:48:31,178
I'm not sure if you all will remember those times.

1168
00:48:31,638 --> 00:48:33,978
Right before my eyes,

1169
00:48:34,308 --> 00:48:35,918
- a car accident happened. - Right.

1170
00:48:36,148 --> 00:48:37,318
- Bam! - Gosh!

1171
00:48:37,648 --> 00:48:39,318
- "Just go." - Right.

1172
00:48:39,318 --> 00:48:41,018
- Right. - Right.

1173
00:48:41,018 --> 00:48:42,588
Food was free in most restaurants.

1174
00:48:42,588 --> 00:48:43,618
- Everything was free. - Right.

1175
00:48:43,618 --> 00:48:45,188
(Korea's first win in World Soccer Games! Free jjajangmyeon)

1176
00:48:46,328 --> 00:48:49,228
(Everyone shared the joy of victory without any conditions.)

1177
00:48:50,458 --> 00:48:52,028
- Korea's happiest moment. - Right.

1178
00:48:52,028 --> 00:48:53,868
The vibes were amazing back then.

1179
00:48:55,838 --> 00:48:58,868
(Although 24 years have passed after that moment,)

1180
00:49:00,308 --> 00:49:02,578
(Korea's matchday is always exciting.)

1181
00:49:04,108 --> 00:49:06,648
While living my life,

1182
00:49:06,878 --> 00:49:08,518
I'm someone who doesn't feel that upset about something...

1183
00:49:08,848 --> 00:49:10,918
or that happy about something.

1184
00:49:11,078 --> 00:49:14,148
This is the only thing that makes me feel excited.

1185
00:49:14,288 --> 00:49:15,488
Soccer is...

1186
00:49:15,618 --> 00:49:16,858
Sung Woo loves soccer.

1187
00:49:17,918 --> 00:49:19,558
It's a moment that comes every four years.

1188
00:49:20,258 --> 00:49:22,058
We can be as loud as we want.

1189
00:49:22,698 --> 00:49:24,528
It's perfectly soundproof as well.

1190
00:49:24,958 --> 00:49:27,028
I came to my studio.

1191
00:49:27,128 --> 00:49:28,668
Oh, your studio?

1192
00:49:28,698 --> 00:49:30,468
No one will hear anything no matter how loud I am.

1193
00:49:30,468 --> 00:49:33,308
- I see. - That's why you're going there.

1194
00:49:35,138 --> 00:49:37,138
(Looking around)

1195
00:49:37,138 --> 00:49:38,848
Why can't I see any red shirts?

1196
00:49:39,508 --> 00:49:40,708
- There wasn't a single red shirt. - Right.

1197
00:49:40,708 --> 00:49:41,918
I used to see 1 or 2 red shirts...

1198
00:49:41,918 --> 00:49:43,148
- in the past. - Right.

1199
00:49:43,148 --> 00:49:44,818
- There should be a few. - That was around...

1200
00:49:44,818 --> 00:49:45,988
- one hour before the match. - It's much different now.

1201
00:49:45,988 --> 00:49:47,948
- It's not like the past these days. - There should be a few then.

1202
00:49:47,948 --> 00:49:49,558
- The match was in the morning. - Right.

1203
00:49:52,788 --> 00:49:54,128
Emergency!

1204
00:49:54,558 --> 00:49:56,258
There should be a little bit of red.

1205
00:49:56,998 --> 00:49:59,098
Everyone is wearing black.

1206
00:50:00,198 --> 00:50:01,728
I thought to myself, "What's going on?"

1207
00:50:02,298 --> 00:50:05,668
It usually started a week before the World Soccer Games.

1208
00:50:05,838 --> 00:50:06,838
Right.

1209
00:50:07,038 --> 00:50:09,138
It was when I was a 7th-grader in 2002.

1210
00:50:09,378 --> 00:50:11,378
There was a very tough man...

1211
00:50:11,908 --> 00:50:14,378
in our apartment complex.

1212
00:50:15,008 --> 00:50:17,478
When Korea made it to the semifinals,

1213
00:50:17,478 --> 00:50:19,388
he smashed his own car.

1214
00:50:20,048 --> 00:50:21,548
He let the young ones smash his car.

1215
00:50:21,548 --> 00:50:23,018
"You can smash my car."

1216
00:50:23,118 --> 00:50:24,318
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1217
00:50:24,818 --> 00:50:27,388
- Right. I remember those times. - I remember those times.

1218
00:50:27,388 --> 00:50:28,498
(The night of madness in 2002 forgave everything.)

1219
00:50:28,498 --> 00:50:29,758
Everything was forgivable.

1220
00:50:30,228 --> 00:50:33,998
Red jerseys started to appear.

1221
00:50:34,498 --> 00:50:37,498
You could feel festival vibes...

1222
00:50:37,498 --> 00:50:39,138
starting to emerge.

1223
00:50:39,138 --> 00:50:40,708
(Festival vibes)

1224
00:50:41,068 --> 00:50:43,908
(Any religion, including the church and temple)

1225
00:50:43,908 --> 00:50:45,308
(Any place, including a funeral hall)

1226
00:50:45,308 --> 00:50:46,678
- The funeral hall! - The funeral hall!

1227
00:50:46,678 --> 00:50:48,108
That was hilarious.

1228
00:50:49,118 --> 00:50:50,448
(Everyone enjoyed 2002 with the same heart.)

1229
00:50:50,448 --> 00:50:52,188
This brings back so many memories.

1230
00:50:52,188 --> 00:50:53,448
(The memories of those times cannot be forgotten.)

1231
00:50:53,448 --> 00:50:55,388
- It was a miracle. - That moment will never come again.

1232
00:50:55,388 --> 00:50:56,418
It will never come.

1233
00:50:56,918 --> 00:50:59,128
It's the only thing we can boast about...

1234
00:50:59,228 --> 00:51:00,528
to the young ones.

1235
00:51:01,328 --> 00:51:04,058
I wasn't able to feel that this year.

1236
00:51:04,398 --> 00:51:05,968
Even on the day of the match,

1237
00:51:06,128 --> 00:51:09,668
it felt like I was the only one on earth to wear a red jersey.

1238
00:51:10,498 --> 00:51:13,368
I wondered for a while if the match was at 10pm.

1239
00:51:13,368 --> 00:51:14,438
(Laughing)

1240
00:51:15,838 --> 00:51:17,278
(Flustered)

1241
00:51:17,278 --> 00:51:18,778
Since there wasn't a single red shirt,

1242
00:51:18,778 --> 00:51:20,548
- you must've doubted yourself. - I didn't see a single red shirt.

1243
00:51:20,548 --> 00:51:21,578
- Right. - Not even one.

1244
00:51:22,348 --> 00:51:24,878
(He arrives feeling a lot of worry.)

1245
00:51:25,288 --> 00:51:26,488
I feel a bit embarrassed.

1246
00:51:27,518 --> 00:51:28,958
It feels like I'm the only one excited.

1247
00:51:30,488 --> 00:51:32,788
People might've thought you have come to sell things.

1248
00:51:32,788 --> 00:51:34,688
(Both hands are filled with cheering items.)

1249
00:51:35,858 --> 00:51:37,858
(Looking around)

1250
00:51:38,998 --> 00:51:40,128
(Why isn't there a single red shirt?)

1251
00:51:40,128 --> 00:51:41,398
Why is it so empty?

1252
00:51:41,598 --> 00:51:44,668
- There isn't a single one. - This is strange.

1253
00:51:45,138 --> 00:51:47,238
It was a lot different from the past.

1254
00:51:48,338 --> 00:51:49,538
Hello.

1255
00:51:49,538 --> 00:51:52,048
Welcome!

1256
00:51:52,708 --> 00:51:55,248
It's a chicken place that I went past often.

1257
00:51:55,548 --> 00:51:57,518
After seeing the chicken place open in the morning,

1258
00:51:57,648 --> 00:51:59,288
I realized it was matchday.

1259
00:51:59,288 --> 00:52:01,118
It was actually the day of the soccer festival.

1260
00:52:01,348 --> 00:52:03,918
- Right. They open on matchdays. - Right.

1261
00:52:04,818 --> 00:52:06,188
It's matchday today, right?

1262
00:52:06,188 --> 00:52:08,288
- Right. - This isn't our opening hours,

1263
00:52:08,288 --> 00:52:09,628
but we got a lot of calls.

1264
00:52:09,628 --> 00:52:10,828
- You got a lot of calls? - Yes.

1265
00:52:11,128 --> 00:52:13,868
I was the only one in a red shirt on the street.

1266
00:52:14,228 --> 00:52:15,568
I felt a bit embarrassed.

1267
00:52:16,138 --> 00:52:17,938
Will you take a look at the menu?

1268
00:52:18,498 --> 00:52:21,768
The garlic rotisserie chicken, soy sauce chicken,

1269
00:52:21,978 --> 00:52:23,508
and the soup tteokbokki.

1270
00:52:23,738 --> 00:52:24,738
That sounds good.

1271
00:52:26,448 --> 00:52:28,578
- Thank you. - Thank you. Enjoy the food.

1272
00:52:28,578 --> 00:52:29,918
Thank you.

1273
00:52:30,948 --> 00:52:33,318
- Thank you. Enjoy the food. - Thank you.

1274
00:52:33,318 --> 00:52:35,048
(He heads to his studio with both hands filled with chicken.)

1275
00:52:35,048 --> 00:52:36,488
That must taste great.

1276
00:52:36,618 --> 00:52:38,828
I leave some seasoned chicken the day before the match.

1277
00:52:38,828 --> 00:52:39,828
On purpose. Right.

1278
00:52:39,828 --> 00:52:42,228
- I always leave some. - Right. Chicken and rice.

1279
00:52:42,358 --> 00:52:44,928
- The meat should be separated. - Of course.

1280
00:52:45,968 --> 00:52:47,228
(He arrives at his studio with morning chicken.)

1281
00:52:47,228 --> 00:52:48,298
Okay.

1282
00:52:48,298 --> 00:52:50,138
(He arrives at his studio with morning chicken.)

1283
00:52:51,068 --> 00:52:54,708
(The studio is already open.)

1284
00:52:55,008 --> 00:52:56,738
(Chuckling)

1285
00:52:56,738 --> 00:52:57,738
Yo!

1286
00:52:58,238 --> 00:52:59,648
(I'm here.)

1287
00:52:59,648 --> 00:53:01,278
- There are people there already. - There are people there already.

1288
00:53:01,808 --> 00:53:02,818
- Who are they? - Who are they?

1289
00:53:02,818 --> 00:53:03,878
(Who has come?)

1290
00:53:05,078 --> 00:53:06,088
Yo!

1291
00:53:06,648 --> 00:53:08,048
(I'm here.)

1292
00:53:08,048 --> 00:53:09,888
- There are people there already. - There are people there already.

1293
00:53:10,018 --> 00:53:11,018
- Who are they? - Who are they?

1294
00:53:11,018 --> 00:53:13,058
- We brought some coffee. - It's the members of Epik High.

1295
00:53:13,358 --> 00:53:14,528
(Mithra, Tukutz, Tablo)

1296
00:53:14,528 --> 00:53:15,998
The members of Epik High!

1297
00:53:15,998 --> 00:53:17,498
- Epik High! - The legends!

1298
00:53:18,898 --> 00:53:21,968
(They have an impressive list of awards.)

1299
00:53:22,598 --> 00:53:23,738
(They made their debut in 2003...)

1300
00:53:23,738 --> 00:53:25,468
(and have an unrivaled musicality that is loved by all generations.)

1301
00:53:26,168 --> 00:53:29,478
(Korea's representative hip-hop group, Epik High)

1302
00:53:29,808 --> 00:53:33,248
When I first started making music,

1303
00:53:33,678 --> 00:53:36,678
they were the first ones to notice my potential.

1304
00:53:36,678 --> 00:53:39,488
They gave me the opportunity to make music.

1305
00:53:40,418 --> 00:53:42,418
They helped me so much.

1306
00:53:42,418 --> 00:53:44,418
A few of the instruments here...

1307
00:53:44,788 --> 00:53:46,458
were used by Tukutz...

1308
00:53:46,458 --> 00:53:48,288
and given to me as gifts.

1309
00:53:48,428 --> 00:53:49,728
(That's awesome.)

1310
00:53:49,728 --> 00:53:51,698
They're the ones you feel grateful for.

1311
00:53:52,298 --> 00:53:54,168
It's the same in the comedy world.

1312
00:53:54,428 --> 00:53:56,168
There are props that seniors like...

1313
00:53:56,168 --> 00:53:57,938
- Shim Hyung Rae used. - Right.

1314
00:53:57,938 --> 00:53:59,238
They feel different.

1315
00:53:59,708 --> 00:54:01,568
- It gives you confidence. - Those are hard to find as well.

1316
00:54:01,568 --> 00:54:02,708
- Right. - Did you get things from Oh Jae Mi?

1317
00:54:02,708 --> 00:54:05,878
The passwords they used or the Wi-Fi system.

1318
00:54:06,078 --> 00:54:08,508
None of the passwords were changed at all.

1319
00:54:08,508 --> 00:54:10,748
Nothing has changed from their time here.

1320
00:54:11,018 --> 00:54:13,888
It's just a bit cleaner than before.

1321
00:54:14,488 --> 00:54:18,318
I kept everything the same because of them.

1322
00:54:20,188 --> 00:54:21,328
(When CODE KUNST was buying the chicken...)

1323
00:54:21,328 --> 00:54:22,528
(Yawning)

1324
00:54:22,698 --> 00:54:25,258
