1330
00:54:38,338 --> 00:54:40,148
- This place feels familiar. - Doesn't it feel like home?

1331
00:54:40,878 --> 00:54:43,278
- What? - Our card bills still come here.

1332
00:54:44,418 --> 00:54:45,718
The card bills are sent there?

1333
00:54:46,488 --> 00:54:47,518
- What? - Tablo!

1334
00:54:47,518 --> 00:54:49,458
Why are you wearing black?

1335
00:54:49,688 --> 00:54:51,518
- What? - Why wear a black shirt?

1336
00:54:51,518 --> 00:54:54,258
Right. It's the day of the match.

1337
00:54:54,628 --> 00:54:55,628
Well...

1338
00:54:55,828 --> 00:54:58,328
Mithra definitely would've felt...

1339
00:54:58,828 --> 00:55:00,098
- guilty inside. - Right.

1340
00:55:00,198 --> 00:55:02,298
But he would've thought, "I'm still wearing a similar color."

1341
00:55:02,298 --> 00:55:03,298
As it's a similar shade.

1342
00:55:03,298 --> 00:55:04,838
- I'm 100 percent certain. - Right.

1343
00:55:04,998 --> 00:55:06,208
That's why he's staying quiet.

1344
00:55:08,108 --> 00:55:11,108
(Tablo is the only one in a different shade.)

1345
00:55:11,438 --> 00:55:13,348
- Come on. - We must all become Red Devils.

1346
00:55:13,348 --> 00:55:16,148
Isn't it fine if my heart is a Red Devil?

1347
00:55:16,348 --> 00:55:18,418
Today, you have to be a Red Devil outside.

1348
00:55:19,088 --> 00:55:20,918
(Tablo's outfit is disappointing.)

1349
00:55:20,918 --> 00:55:21,948
I brought some jerseys.

1350
00:55:21,948 --> 00:55:23,788
- Lend me one then. - Right.

1351
00:55:23,788 --> 00:55:26,388
- Did you bring theirs? - That was why I brought a few.

1352
00:55:26,828 --> 00:55:28,458
I don't know a lot about soccer.

1353
00:55:28,658 --> 00:55:30,428
I just watch the World Soccer Games.

1354
00:55:30,428 --> 00:55:32,268
- That's the best. - It's Park Ji Sung's jersey!

1355
00:55:32,268 --> 00:55:34,228
(It's Park Ji Sung's jersey!)

1356
00:55:34,428 --> 00:55:36,168
- Tablo should wear it then. - Right.

1357
00:55:36,168 --> 00:55:37,168
Right.

1358
00:55:37,438 --> 00:55:39,138
He used to be known for looking like Park Ji Sung.

1359
00:55:39,338 --> 00:55:40,738
- Right. - Park Ji Sung.

1360
00:55:41,338 --> 00:55:42,838
- Right. - Right.

1361
00:55:42,838 --> 00:55:44,478
- He was known for that. - Right.

1362
00:55:45,338 --> 00:55:46,378
Here you are.

1363
00:55:46,378 --> 00:55:47,378
(Here you are, Park Ji Sung.)

1364
00:55:47,378 --> 00:55:49,548
- "Here you are." - You asked why I brought them.

1365
00:55:49,548 --> 00:55:50,748
Now, you look the most interested.

1366
00:55:50,748 --> 00:55:52,248
- Yes! - He loves it.

1367
00:55:52,248 --> 00:55:53,718
(Excited)

1368
00:55:53,718 --> 00:55:56,218
- It's different with a jersey on. - Think about it.

1369
00:55:56,218 --> 00:55:57,818
- Right. - Imagine going to a game...

1370
00:55:57,818 --> 00:55:58,988
in a regular outfit.

1371
00:55:58,988 --> 00:56:00,258
- That can't happen. - Your heart won't click.

1372
00:56:00,258 --> 00:56:02,028
- It won't match the vibe. - You must follow the dress code.

1373
00:56:02,028 --> 00:56:04,428
Why are you wearing so many layers indoors?

1374
00:56:04,828 --> 00:56:05,998
It's cold here.

1375
00:56:06,328 --> 00:56:08,668
It fits you a lot better than I thought.

1376
00:56:09,468 --> 00:56:11,338
I'm not fat!

1377
00:56:12,308 --> 00:56:14,608
It's a stereotype that people have about me.

1378
00:56:14,608 --> 00:56:17,208
People have a misunderstanding that I'm really big.

1379
00:56:17,678 --> 00:56:20,048
- He lost a lot of weight. - He said he lost a lot of weight.

1380
00:56:20,378 --> 00:56:21,448
(He shows off the cheering items he brought from home.)

1381
00:56:21,448 --> 00:56:24,318
(Blowing)

1382
00:56:29,118 --> 00:56:30,188
Don't blow that.

1383
00:56:30,188 --> 00:56:31,418
(Laughing)

1384
00:56:31,418 --> 00:56:32,458
Did you hear me?

1385
00:56:33,958 --> 00:56:36,398
I was going to watch it quietly at home.

1386
00:56:36,398 --> 00:56:37,398
You can't do that.

1387
00:56:37,398 --> 00:56:39,028
Soccer must be watched with a lot of noise.

1388
00:56:39,128 --> 00:56:40,728
- It must be loud with soccer. - Right.

1389
00:56:40,968 --> 00:56:42,438
Soccer must be watched in a wild atmosphere.

1390
00:56:42,438 --> 00:56:44,338
That's a great line. "Soccer must be watched with a lot of noise."

1391
00:56:45,938 --> 00:56:47,408
I can't click with you right now.

1392
00:56:47,408 --> 00:56:49,438
That means he wants me to blow it one more time.

1393
00:56:49,508 --> 00:56:51,238
(Blowing)

1394
00:56:51,238 --> 00:56:52,878
Are you sure?

1395
00:56:53,978 --> 00:56:56,948
I've spent a lot of time with them.

1396
00:56:56,978 --> 00:56:58,818
You understand the Epik High language?

1397
00:56:58,818 --> 00:57:00,088
Right.

1398
00:57:00,588 --> 00:57:02,118
Don't blow that.

1399
00:57:02,118 --> 00:57:04,318
(Just enjoy it.)

1400
00:57:04,318 --> 00:57:06,258
Don't blow that.

1401
00:57:06,628 --> 00:57:07,858
"Please blow it."

1402
00:57:07,858 --> 00:57:09,228
(Translation)

1403
00:57:09,458 --> 00:57:10,558
(Blowing)

1404
00:57:10,858 --> 00:57:12,158
What is that? Is that a vuvuzela?

1405
00:57:12,698 --> 00:57:14,398
- Give me one. - See?

1406
00:57:14,398 --> 00:57:16,238
Why would you blow that indoors?

1407
00:57:16,398 --> 00:57:19,168
Isn't he a representative celebrity soccer freak?

1408
00:57:19,268 --> 00:57:21,408
You're going to watch Park Ji Sung's commentary, right?

1409
00:57:21,538 --> 00:57:22,538
Of course.

1410
00:57:22,538 --> 00:57:24,738
(Of course.)

1411
00:57:24,908 --> 00:57:26,078
He's watching himself.

1412
00:57:26,078 --> 00:57:27,508
(The Park Ji Sung lookalike confidently takes his seat.)

1413
00:57:28,008 --> 00:57:29,478
Power!

1414
00:57:29,778 --> 00:57:31,048
I gave it to Tukutz.

1415
00:57:31,218 --> 00:57:32,548
- It's mine. - Gosh, it looks nice.

1416
00:57:33,718 --> 00:57:35,388
Is this the one G-DRAGON made?

1417
00:57:35,548 --> 00:57:37,958
(Limited edition jacket collaborated with GD)

1418
00:57:37,958 --> 00:57:39,628
I want to wear that.

1419
00:57:39,628 --> 00:57:41,258
Power!

1420
00:57:41,258 --> 00:57:43,498
I gave it to Tukutz.

1421
00:57:44,498 --> 00:57:46,798
No! Give it to me if it was made by G-DRAGON.

1422
00:57:46,798 --> 00:57:47,868
It's mine!

1423
00:57:48,028 --> 00:57:49,298
We heard, "It's mine!"

1424
00:57:49,298 --> 00:57:50,398
You're not actually giving it to him, right?

1425
00:57:50,398 --> 00:57:51,498
I am.

1426
00:57:52,268 --> 00:57:53,668
He looks so excited.

1427
00:57:53,668 --> 00:57:55,238
That's hard to get.

1428
00:57:56,008 --> 00:57:57,678
(You're not actually giving it to him, right?)

1429
00:57:57,678 --> 00:57:59,348
(I am.)

1430
00:57:59,348 --> 00:58:01,748
- Well... - We gave you this TV.

1431
00:58:01,848 --> 00:58:03,918
- So... - "We?" I bought it.

1432
00:58:03,918 --> 00:58:05,718
- I bought this TV. - I bought it.

1433
00:58:05,718 --> 00:58:07,348
- I bought it. - It's mine.

1434
00:58:07,348 --> 00:58:09,458
- I bought it for you! - I bought it!

1435
00:58:09,458 --> 00:58:10,788
- I bought it for you! - I bought it!

1436
00:58:10,788 --> 00:58:12,188
- Wait. - It's mine.

1437
00:58:12,188 --> 00:58:13,358
Get out your receipt.

1438
00:58:13,358 --> 00:58:14,888
- I bought it for you. - You bought it?

1439
00:58:15,858 --> 00:58:17,598
- They're so childish. - Fourth-graders!

1440
00:58:17,598 --> 00:58:18,658
They're just like fourth-graders.

1441
00:58:18,658 --> 00:58:21,228
Are they fathers of children or children?

1442
00:58:21,228 --> 00:58:23,168
(Confused)

1443
00:58:23,168 --> 00:58:24,398
- You bought it? - Gosh!

1444
00:58:24,398 --> 00:58:25,668
Get out your receipt.

1445
00:58:25,668 --> 00:58:27,208
- I bought it for you! - You bought it?

1446
00:58:27,208 --> 00:58:28,808
I bought this for you as a gift...

1447
00:58:28,808 --> 00:58:30,278
for coming into this studio.

1448
00:58:30,538 --> 00:58:32,208
Gosh. I should never buy things...

1449
00:58:32,208 --> 00:58:33,748
- for a friend. - He got it back from him.

1450
00:58:33,748 --> 00:58:36,178
Hey, did I leave that fridge for you?

1451
00:58:36,648 --> 00:58:37,648
Yes.

1452
00:58:37,648 --> 00:58:39,248
CODE KUNST gave the jacket to Tablo.

1453
00:58:40,188 --> 00:58:42,118
It should be given to the one who bought the TV.

1454
00:58:42,118 --> 00:58:44,188
- Hey. - Tablo was the one to buy it.

1455
00:58:44,188 --> 00:58:46,128
But how can you take it away from him?

1456
00:58:46,288 --> 00:58:48,358
The one who gave the TV deserves it.

1457
00:58:48,358 --> 00:58:49,458
It must be done accurately.

1458
00:58:49,558 --> 00:58:51,858
- His lips are drooping down. - Tablo...

1459
00:58:51,858 --> 00:58:54,398
- His lips are dropping down! - He's upset!

1460
00:58:55,968 --> 00:58:57,038
Take it if you want, Jeong Sik.

1461
00:58:57,038 --> 00:58:58,598
You love G-DRAGON.

1462
00:58:59,268 --> 00:59:01,368
- It's fine. - This won't be released again.

1463
00:59:01,368 --> 00:59:02,508
Gosh, he's going to be upset.

1464
00:59:03,178 --> 00:59:04,538
- I'll give it to you. - Give it to him.

1465
00:59:05,708 --> 00:59:07,078
- I'll give it to you. - Give it to him.

1466
00:59:07,308 --> 00:59:08,608
Gosh.

1467
00:59:08,608 --> 00:59:09,748
- Gosh. - Power!

1468
00:59:09,948 --> 00:59:12,118
- His lips are going up! - His lips are going up!

1469
00:59:12,348 --> 00:59:13,688
- His lips! - They're going up!

1470
00:59:13,888 --> 00:59:15,348
Why get upset?

1471
00:59:15,348 --> 00:59:16,658
- He's going to sing, "Power!" - He went, "Power!"

1472
00:59:16,658 --> 00:59:18,218
(Home sweet home)

1473
00:59:18,218 --> 00:59:19,658
(You were all wrong.)

1474
00:59:20,028 --> 00:59:22,028
- SIK-DRAGON. - SIK-DRAGON.

1475
00:59:22,028 --> 00:59:23,428
(JEONG SIK-DRAGON)

1476
00:59:23,428 --> 00:59:24,558
They're hilarious.

1477
00:59:25,358 --> 00:59:26,928
- We should have some chicken. - Let's set the table.

1478
00:59:26,928 --> 00:59:28,828
We can't eat before the match starts.

1479
00:59:28,998 --> 00:59:29,998
We should eat when the match starts.

1480
00:59:29,998 --> 00:59:31,268
- Why is that? - What?

1481
00:59:31,668 --> 00:59:33,108
- Why is that? - Why is that?

1482
00:59:33,208 --> 00:59:35,268
- Why is that? The food is there. - That's...

1483
00:59:35,638 --> 00:59:36,908
A box of chicken must be eaten before the match starts.

1484
00:59:36,908 --> 00:59:39,878
Right. It should be eaten like an energy bar.

1485
00:59:39,878 --> 00:59:41,148
Enough is enough.

1486
00:59:41,148 --> 00:59:42,348
(Enough is enough in front of the chicken.)

1487
00:59:42,348 --> 00:59:44,178
Whenever I buy food,

1488
00:59:44,318 --> 00:59:47,948
whether it be for a movie, soccer match, or a concert,

1489
00:59:48,518 --> 00:59:50,458
they finish everything before it starts.

1490
00:59:50,618 --> 00:59:51,858
- That's how it is. - That's how it is.

1491
00:59:51,858 --> 00:59:54,328
That's what people usually do.

1492
00:59:54,328 --> 00:59:55,588
The popcorn must be eaten when it's hot.

1493
00:59:55,728 --> 00:59:57,358
But since that always happened,

1494
00:59:57,358 --> 00:59:58,658
I wanted to eat the food while watching the match.

1495
00:59:58,658 --> 01:00:00,298
Why must that happen?

1496
01:00:00,598 --> 01:00:03,068
I wanted to talk with them before the match.

1497
01:00:03,538 --> 01:00:05,068
Why eat after the match starts?

1498
01:00:05,068 --> 01:00:06,538
(Grumbling)

1499
01:00:06,538 --> 01:00:07,738
He's grumbling.

1500
01:00:07,868 --> 01:00:10,008
- See? - He sounds like my grandpa.

1501
01:00:10,278 --> 01:00:11,938
You should have some sauce around your mouth.

1502
01:00:11,938 --> 01:00:13,248
I was wrong, wasn't I?

1503
01:00:13,248 --> 01:00:14,278
- You were wrong. - You were wrong.

1504
01:00:14,278 --> 01:00:16,018
- It's flowing that way. - Right.

1505
01:00:16,148 --> 01:00:17,378
- You can't do that. - Right.

1506
01:00:17,778 --> 01:00:19,318
- You must eat right away. - You can't do that.

1507
01:00:19,618 --> 01:00:20,688
I'm sorry.

1508
01:00:20,688 --> 01:00:22,148
(I'm sorry.)

1509
01:00:22,218 --> 01:00:23,618
We can't eat...

1510
01:00:23,618 --> 01:00:25,218
- before the kick-off? - We can't.

1511
01:00:25,288 --> 01:00:26,358
Even before a movie starts,

1512
01:00:26,358 --> 01:00:28,358
- I finish the popcorn. - Hey, let's eat.

1513
01:00:28,358 --> 01:00:29,758
- It's time for me to eat. - Well...

1514
01:00:29,758 --> 01:00:31,298
(Sensitive)

1515
01:00:31,298 --> 01:00:32,928
(Smacking his lips)

1516
01:00:32,928 --> 01:00:33,998
- Hey! - Prepare the next thing.

1517
01:00:33,998 --> 01:00:36,768
The food is going to go bad after 30 minutes.

1518
01:00:36,768 --> 01:00:38,498
Then let's open one box.

1519
01:00:38,498 --> 01:00:39,938
There was tteokbokki now that I think about it.

1520
01:00:39,938 --> 01:00:41,038
We should eat the tteokbokki as well.

1521
01:00:41,038 --> 01:00:42,608
- Hey. - We won't eat the chicken?

1522
01:00:42,608 --> 01:00:43,838
We can't eat the chicken?

1523
01:00:43,838 --> 01:00:44,838
(A bolt from the blue)

1524
01:00:44,838 --> 01:00:46,748
- Gosh, he's so exhausting. - CODE KUNST is a bit...

1525
01:00:46,748 --> 01:00:48,478
I don't like this place.

1526
01:00:48,848 --> 01:00:51,218
- It must be his superstition. - I have a superstition as well.

1527
01:00:51,218 --> 01:00:52,488
I don't like watching a game like this.

1528
01:00:52,488 --> 01:00:53,948
We'll lose if we do this.

1529
01:00:54,148 --> 01:00:56,118
(Let's cheer our team for 30 minutes.)

1530
01:00:56,118 --> 01:00:57,688
Go, Korea!

1531
01:00:57,688 --> 01:00:59,888
(Go, Korea!)

1532
01:01:00,658 --> 01:01:01,928
Look at Mithra!

1533
01:01:01,928 --> 01:01:02,928
(It's loud and he feels hungry.)

1534
01:01:03,128 --> 01:01:05,698
Don't you have earplugs at the studio?

1535
01:01:07,128 --> 01:01:09,338
It must be like this when watching soccer.

1536
01:01:09,338 --> 01:01:12,708
He's genuinely prepared to watch the soccer match.

1537
01:01:12,708 --> 01:01:15,808
I live for this.

1538
01:01:15,808 --> 01:01:17,708
I'm not joking about this.

1539
01:01:17,708 --> 01:01:19,948
- I always wait for this event. - I'm always like that.

1540
01:01:19,978 --> 01:01:21,978
What are you saying? You didn't even know there was a match today.

1541
01:01:22,108 --> 01:01:23,778
Why are there only three?

1542
01:01:23,778 --> 01:01:27,248
I came from abroad yesterday to watch this here!

1543
01:01:27,248 --> 01:01:28,918
- Really? - It was to watch this here!

1544
01:01:28,918 --> 01:01:30,788
You asked if the games started in September.

1545
01:01:32,558 --> 01:01:34,428
Gosh, I feel so annoyed.

1546
01:01:36,358 --> 01:01:38,358
They get on each other's nerves so well.

1547
01:01:38,358 --> 01:01:40,628
- When did I say that? - Let's take turns to take shots.

1548
01:01:40,628 --> 01:01:43,638
(They're already fighting again.)

1549
01:01:44,738 --> 01:01:45,798
It's actually the World Soccer Games.

1550
01:01:45,798 --> 01:01:46,908
I want to watch it live.

1551
01:01:46,908 --> 01:01:48,908
During the 2002 games,

1552
01:01:49,068 --> 01:01:51,378
I watched the France versus Senegal match...

1553
01:01:51,378 --> 01:01:52,848
- Hold on. - at the stadium.

1554
01:01:52,848 --> 01:01:53,848
Really?

1555
01:01:53,848 --> 01:01:55,808
Did you watch the 2002 games at home?

1556
01:01:56,418 --> 01:01:57,648
- I watched it at the academy. - The academy?

1557
01:01:57,878 --> 01:01:58,948
The English academy.

1558
01:01:58,948 --> 01:02:00,718
(Gosh, you're a baby.)

1559
01:02:00,718 --> 01:02:03,088
- Gosh, you snot-nosed kid. - Gosh.

1560
01:02:03,088 --> 01:02:05,658
Hey, we watched it while drinking beer in Sinchon.

1561
01:02:06,088 --> 01:02:08,328
(Distant memory)

1562
01:02:09,228 --> 01:02:10,498
I'm really jealous.

1563
01:02:10,498 --> 01:02:11,598
I'm really jealous...

1564
01:02:11,598 --> 01:02:12,668
- that they were adults in 2002. - Right.

1565
01:02:12,668 --> 01:02:13,828
- Right. - Right.

1566
01:02:14,198 --> 01:02:15,968
I have a question. What's your score prediction?

1567
01:02:16,668 --> 01:02:18,098
I predict a 3:0 win.

1568
01:02:18,268 --> 01:02:19,908
- A 3:0 win? - A 3:0 win?

1569
01:02:20,308 --> 01:02:21,538
I'm serious about this.

1570
01:02:22,008 --> 01:02:23,838
- I think it will be a 5:1 win. - A 5:1 win?

1571
01:02:23,838 --> 01:02:24,878
- A 5:1 win. - I think it will be a 4:1 win.

1572
01:02:24,878 --> 01:02:26,978
Korea 4, Czech Republic 1.

1573
01:02:26,978 --> 01:02:28,008
Gosh.

1574
01:02:29,348 --> 01:02:30,748
Those were terrible predictions.

1575
01:02:31,118 --> 01:02:33,448
- But... - Hyun Moo's prediction.

1576
01:02:33,948 --> 01:02:34,948
But, Hyun Moo...

1577
01:02:34,948 --> 01:02:35,958
(The one who predicted the 2:1 turnaround win feels relaxed.)

1578
01:02:35,958 --> 01:02:38,118
Do you know why I predicted a 3:0 win?

1579
01:02:38,188 --> 01:02:40,088
It's fun to make a big bet.

1580
01:02:40,088 --> 01:02:42,258
- Right. - I'm not interested about bets.

1581
01:02:42,598 --> 01:02:44,158
I could see 2:1 in my eyes.

1582
01:02:44,558 --> 01:02:46,198
- Sorry? What are you saying? - Gosh.

1583
01:02:46,198 --> 01:02:47,898
On top of that, I predicted the exact score...

1584
01:02:47,898 --> 01:02:49,238
and I guessed that Oh Hyeon Gyu would score.

1585
01:02:49,238 --> 01:02:50,268
Really?

1586
01:02:50,998 --> 01:02:52,768
My nickname is Shaman Jun Hyun Moo right now.

1587
01:02:53,768 --> 01:02:55,068
I'm serious.

1588
01:02:55,608 --> 01:02:57,778
- What about the Mexico game? - The next one.

1589
01:02:57,778 --> 01:02:59,848
Right. We'll admit it if you get this one right.

1590
01:03:00,408 --> 01:03:02,178
- Here's Shaman Jun Hyun Moo. - Shaman Jun Hyun Moo.

1591
01:03:02,178 --> 01:03:03,178
All right.

1592
01:03:03,578 --> 01:03:05,218
My first prediction was 2:2.

1593
01:03:05,218 --> 01:03:06,788
- Which team was 2? - I predicted 2:2.

1594
01:03:06,788 --> 01:03:08,118
- Oh, 2:2. - I see.

1595
01:03:08,488 --> 01:03:10,918
But Mexico's Kim Min Jae got sent off.

1596
01:03:11,288 --> 01:03:12,958
He can't play against Korea.

1597
01:03:13,358 --> 01:03:14,728
That is why I predict it will be a 2:1 win.

1598
01:03:14,928 --> 01:03:16,658
- A 2:1 win? - Korea will win 2:1.

1599
01:03:16,658 --> 01:03:18,058
- It was actually 2:2? - Right.

1600
01:03:18,058 --> 01:03:19,198
What about the scorer of the first goal?

1601
01:03:20,098 --> 01:03:21,398
Must we go in that deep?

1602
01:03:21,398 --> 01:03:22,468
You guessed Oh Hyeon Gyu right.

1603
01:03:22,468 --> 01:03:24,168
You said you saw it with your eyes.

1604
01:03:24,168 --> 01:03:26,168
Tell us what you see.

1605
01:03:26,168 --> 01:03:28,338
- Actually, - Through Shaman Jun's eyes.

1606
01:03:28,338 --> 01:03:30,538
- I see Cho Gue Sung. - Cho Gue Sung?

1607
01:03:30,738 --> 01:03:32,708
There aren't many tall players in the Mexican team,

1608
01:03:32,708 --> 01:03:33,908
so Cho Gue Sung might be used.

1609
01:03:33,908 --> 01:03:34,978
- As a starting member? - In the second half.

1610
01:03:34,978 --> 01:03:36,178
- It sounds convincing. - Oh, in the second half?

1611
01:03:36,178 --> 01:03:37,548
- In the 2nd half. - In the 2nd half.

1612
01:03:37,548 --> 01:03:39,178
Then will Korea score first?

1613
01:03:39,448 --> 01:03:41,188
- I can't see about that. - You can't?

1614
01:03:41,188 --> 01:03:42,618
There are things that even shamans can't see.

1615
01:03:42,888 --> 01:03:45,188
- What are you talking about? - That's so convenient.

1616
01:03:45,188 --> 01:03:46,958
There are things that even shamans can't see.

1617
01:03:47,958 --> 01:03:49,598
(Unfortunately, he failed to predict the result.)

1618
01:03:49,598 --> 01:03:51,498
Even just the talk about it makes us excited.

1619
01:03:51,498 --> 01:03:52,728
- I know. - I know. Me too.

1620
01:03:52,998 --> 01:03:54,798
Then let's bet on the specifics.

1621
01:03:54,798 --> 01:03:56,968
The first goal from Korea.

1622
01:03:57,138 --> 01:03:58,398
I think it'll be from Lee Kang In.

1623
01:03:58,538 --> 01:03:59,638
No.

1624
01:03:59,768 --> 01:04:02,268
What do you mean no? I think he'll score.

1625
01:04:02,638 --> 01:04:03,778
The first goal...

1626
01:04:05,608 --> 01:04:06,678
will be from Hwang In Beom.

1627
01:04:06,808 --> 01:04:07,978
That sounds possible.

1628
01:04:08,308 --> 01:04:09,418
This is the difference between...

1629
01:04:09,418 --> 01:04:11,118
a knowledgeable fan and a clueless fan.

1630
01:04:11,648 --> 01:04:12,718
Son Heung Min and Lee Kang In...

1631
01:04:12,718 --> 01:04:14,188
- are a pair. - That's right.

1632
01:04:14,188 --> 01:04:16,418
- Only the players. - The current lineup is the best.

1633
01:04:21,428 --> 01:04:22,528
Let's go.

1634
01:04:22,528 --> 01:04:24,398
(Everyone gets up.)

1635
01:04:24,398 --> 01:04:25,698
- Let's go. - Gosh, the national anthem.

1636
01:04:26,098 --> 01:04:27,828
- When the song plays, - With deep respect.

1637
01:04:27,828 --> 01:04:29,168
everyone listens with deep respect.

1638
01:04:29,368 --> 01:04:30,968
This is a must.

1639
01:04:31,198 --> 01:04:32,338
- It makes you excited. - Five to one.

1640
01:04:33,138 --> 01:04:34,338
Three to zero.

1641
01:04:34,908 --> 01:04:36,138
The mecca of street cheering.

1642
01:04:36,278 --> 01:04:40,078
(A sea of red gathered at Gwanghwamun Square as one.)

1643
01:04:41,048 --> 01:04:42,678
(Let's go, Korea!)

1644
01:04:42,678 --> 01:04:45,248
(Clapping)

1645
01:04:46,248 --> 01:04:47,388
(The four gathered at a different place but with the same heart.)

1646
01:04:47,388 --> 01:04:48,648
- Two to one. - Okay.

1647
01:04:49,318 --> 01:04:52,058
(5 minutes before the game starts)

1648
01:04:52,058 --> 01:04:53,188
I have a good feeling, though.

1649
01:04:53,288 --> 01:04:54,388
- Yes. - It's not bad, right?

1650
01:04:54,388 --> 01:04:56,858
- I have a good feeling. - Seeing how the coach...

1651
01:04:56,858 --> 01:04:59,158
has the same hairstyle as mine, I think it's going to go well.

1652
01:04:59,158 --> 01:05:00,468
- They do look similar. - They look similar.

1653
01:05:00,568 --> 01:05:02,028
- You know that feeling. - I have a good feeling.

1654
01:05:02,498 --> 01:05:04,268
When the coaches had...

1655
01:05:04,268 --> 01:05:07,368
similar hairstyles as Tukutz for the World Soccer Games,

1656
01:05:07,368 --> 01:05:08,808
Korea always did well.

1657
01:05:09,378 --> 01:05:10,738
There's such a belief?

1658
01:05:11,338 --> 01:05:12,508
Are they playing?

1659
01:05:12,638 --> 01:05:14,108
- Hold on. - Number 19.

1660
01:05:14,108 --> 01:05:15,308
- Number 19. - He lifted it.

1661
01:05:15,508 --> 01:05:16,718
- He's playing. - I can eat...

1662
01:05:16,718 --> 01:05:17,878
as soon as they kick off, right?

1663
01:05:17,878 --> 01:05:19,518
- Yes. - I can get ready ahead, right?

1664
01:05:19,518 --> 01:05:20,588
That's right.

1665
01:05:20,588 --> 01:05:21,588
It's Paik Seung Ho.

1666
01:05:21,588 --> 01:05:22,618
But you can't put it in your mouth.

1667
01:05:23,158 --> 01:05:24,188
All right.

1668
01:05:24,188 --> 01:05:25,818
(Come on.)

1669
01:05:25,818 --> 01:05:26,828
My goodness.

1670
01:05:26,828 --> 01:05:29,428
This is the fun part. The fun part has started.

1671
01:05:29,428 --> 01:05:30,628
(Shameless)

1672
01:05:31,698 --> 01:05:33,428
- Is it okay if my spit gets on it? - No.

1673
01:05:33,428 --> 01:05:34,668
My younger brother, have a bite first.

1674
01:05:34,668 --> 01:05:36,298
- You can't taste it. - As soon as they kick off...

1675
01:05:36,298 --> 01:05:37,568
- It's started. - They can eat now.

1676
01:05:37,568 --> 01:05:38,768
(The first half has started.)

1677
01:05:38,768 --> 01:05:39,808
Take a bite.

1678
01:05:39,808 --> 01:05:40,968
It's started. You can eat now.

1679
01:05:40,968 --> 01:05:42,708
(Taking a big bite)

1680
01:05:43,738 --> 01:05:45,808
You see? Something fun happens if you wait.

1681
01:05:45,808 --> 01:05:47,478
This is really fun.

1682
01:05:47,708 --> 01:05:49,918
It does look fun because you ate after the whistle.

1683
01:05:51,018 --> 01:05:53,218
It must be more delicious since they were starved.

1684
01:05:53,218 --> 01:05:55,488
(They finally taste the fried chicken after the match started.)

1685
01:05:55,948 --> 01:05:57,818
Are you on the winning side or the losing side...

1686
01:05:57,818 --> 01:05:58,858
when you cheer for your team?

1687
01:05:59,388 --> 01:06:01,588
- When I cheer for them, - They lose.

1688
01:06:01,588 --> 01:06:02,658
they lose for sure.

1689
01:06:03,658 --> 01:06:04,858
We're done for.

1690
01:06:06,268 --> 01:06:08,268
But when the three of us gathered and watched, they always won.

1691
01:06:08,498 --> 01:06:09,898
- Is that so? - When three of us meet, they win.

1692
01:06:09,898 --> 01:06:11,568
I'm mostly on the winning side too.

1693
01:06:12,198 --> 01:06:14,468
- They're warmed up. - Actually, when we watched,

1694
01:06:14,738 --> 01:06:17,278
they always scored when I went to the bathroom.

1695
01:06:17,278 --> 01:06:18,308
That's true.

1696
01:06:18,308 --> 01:06:20,308
There are people who claim the team loses...

1697
01:06:20,308 --> 01:06:22,308
- when they watch the game. - That's right.

1698
01:06:22,308 --> 01:06:24,978
- I had one big incident, though. - What is it?

1699
01:06:24,978 --> 01:06:27,188
During the match against Italy in the 2002 World Soccer Game,

1700
01:06:27,548 --> 01:06:30,288
I turned around and left when I thought they lost.

1701
01:06:30,458 --> 01:06:31,818
But Seol Ki Hyeon...

1702
01:06:31,818 --> 01:06:33,158
- score the equalizer. - The equalizer.

1703
01:06:33,158 --> 01:06:34,328
You shouldn't watch then.

1704
01:06:34,928 --> 01:06:36,498
- I shouldn't watch? - He shouldn't watch?

1705
01:06:36,758 --> 01:06:38,598
Please sleep during the match against Mexico.

1706
01:06:39,358 --> 01:06:40,528
Seon Min, please sleep.

1707
01:06:40,528 --> 01:06:42,428
- Yes, please go crash. - Just sleep.

1708
01:06:42,898 --> 01:06:44,068
You should go to sleep.

1709
01:06:45,968 --> 01:06:47,108
Let's go.

1710
01:06:48,208 --> 01:06:50,178
- It's Seol Young Woo, right? - Let's score directly from a cross.

1711
01:06:52,008 --> 01:06:54,878
(They continue to chew with their eyes fixed on the TV.)

1712
01:06:55,078 --> 01:06:58,318
It doesn't look bad, though. I think Team Korea is more agile.

1713
01:06:58,318 --> 01:06:59,648
- We have better energy. - I know.

1714
01:06:59,918 --> 01:07:01,418
Why can't we see the match, though?

1715
01:07:01,618 --> 01:07:03,618
We can't watch the match because of copyright restrictions.

1716
01:07:03,788 --> 01:07:05,618
You should watch while imagining the game.

1717
01:07:05,618 --> 01:07:07,828
You guys can play it in your head, can't you?

1718
01:07:08,728 --> 01:07:09,858
The Czech team...

1719
01:07:09,858 --> 01:07:11,558
- is physically strong. - It's a bummer.

1720
01:07:11,758 --> 01:07:14,268
- They're strong. - They're tall too.

1721
01:07:14,568 --> 01:07:16,168
Their average height is 190cm.

1722
01:07:17,098 --> 01:07:19,338
I wonder how it'd feel to live as a tall person like him.

1723
01:07:20,308 --> 01:07:21,438
They say it's inconvenient.

1724
01:07:22,568 --> 01:07:23,608
It's inconvenient.

1725
01:07:23,908 --> 01:07:25,238
- Their knees hurt too. - I bet it's inconvenient...

1726
01:07:25,238 --> 01:07:26,548
- on planes. - Of course.

1727
01:07:26,778 --> 01:07:27,878
Their knees hurt too.

1728
01:07:29,108 --> 01:07:30,148
I hope they fall.

1729
01:07:31,218 --> 01:07:32,948
- That's so... - That's blunt.

1730
01:07:32,948 --> 01:07:34,388
It's really blunt and simple.

1731
01:07:34,988 --> 01:07:37,258
I get where that comes from.

1732
01:07:37,588 --> 01:07:40,788
Also, it's important to cheer like that.

1733
01:07:41,028 --> 01:07:44,458
- I've seen worse. - For me, when I watch the game,

1734
01:07:44,458 --> 01:07:45,628
I do this instead of talking.

1735
01:07:45,628 --> 01:07:48,298
When the ball goes over the goal line,

1736
01:07:48,528 --> 01:07:50,398
or when I wish it to go over the line,

1737
01:07:50,398 --> 01:07:52,598
I'd suck in the air like this.

1738
01:07:53,568 --> 01:07:54,738
Like this.

1739
01:07:54,838 --> 01:07:55,868
- So the ball goes over the line? - When I wish it...

1740
01:07:55,868 --> 01:07:56,908
to go the other way,

1741
01:07:57,278 --> 01:07:58,408
I do this.

1742
01:07:58,538 --> 01:08:00,478
(That's right.)

1743
01:08:00,848 --> 01:08:02,978
But it's sort of effective.

1744
01:08:02,978 --> 01:08:04,918
- What? It works? - Yes, it works for real.

1745
01:08:05,248 --> 01:08:07,218
- Your energy is sent. - My energy is sent.

1746
01:08:07,218 --> 01:08:08,288
My gosh.

1747
01:08:09,048 --> 01:08:10,988
It actually works. Try it.

1748
01:08:10,988 --> 01:08:12,318
That's so like MINHO.

1749
01:08:13,728 --> 01:08:15,258
They should score one now if they're to score five.

1750
01:08:15,258 --> 01:08:16,328
- What? - What?

1751
01:08:16,928 --> 01:08:18,598
Hey, that's... That one's going in!

1752
01:08:20,168 --> 01:08:21,768
- Here we go. - Wait, they're almost there!

1753
01:08:21,768 --> 01:08:24,498
- It's going in! - Goal!

1754
01:08:24,498 --> 01:08:25,568
Gosh!

1755
01:08:25,638 --> 01:08:26,808
What a loss!

1756
01:08:27,108 --> 01:08:29,168
Someone should've been standing there!

1757
01:08:29,168 --> 01:08:32,308
(Someone should've been standing there!)

1758
01:08:32,908 --> 01:08:35,208
You become a coach when you watch a game.

1759
01:08:35,208 --> 01:08:37,048
Everyone becomes a coach when you watch it from home.

1760
01:08:37,048 --> 01:08:39,318
- You'd point at them too. - This is hilarious.

1761
01:08:41,788 --> 01:08:42,918
- Hey! - What was that?

1762
01:08:43,088 --> 01:08:44,718
- That's right. - The referee didn't give a foul.

1763
01:08:44,718 --> 01:08:45,788
A foul.

1764
01:08:45,788 --> 01:08:46,858
- Why not give a foul? - When he fell?

1765
01:08:46,858 --> 01:08:48,158
- Why didn't he give a foul? - It's when Lee Kang In fell, right?

1766
01:08:48,158 --> 01:08:50,228
- He basically threw him. - The situation like this...

1767
01:08:50,228 --> 01:08:53,168
We're watching them watching a soccer match.

1768
01:08:53,868 --> 01:08:55,198
- It's so weird. - Right.

1769
01:08:55,528 --> 01:08:57,198
And the viewers are watching us.

1770
01:08:57,198 --> 01:08:59,298
- The viewers are watching us... - Everyone is watching each other.

1771
01:08:59,398 --> 01:09:01,408
- It could feel frustrating. - watching CODE KUNST...

1772
01:09:01,408 --> 01:09:02,738
- watching a soccer game. - It's so weird.

1773
01:09:02,868 --> 01:09:04,708
It's a three-layer watching.

1774
01:09:06,178 --> 01:09:07,978
The viewers are watching us watching the three of them...

1775
01:09:07,978 --> 01:09:09,308
watching a game.

1776
01:09:09,918 --> 01:09:11,418
What on earth is happening?

1777
01:09:11,418 --> 01:09:13,318
(A third-level observer's viewpoint?)

1778
01:09:14,188 --> 01:09:16,488
- Why? Why not give a foul? - What? Why didn't he give a foul?

1779
01:09:16,488 --> 01:09:18,058
He basically threw him.

1780
01:09:18,858 --> 01:09:20,828
- To the outside... - Referee, move!

1781
01:09:22,858 --> 01:09:24,398
I didn't like that jerk from the start.

1782
01:09:27,798 --> 01:09:29,168
(Embarrassed)

1783
01:09:29,168 --> 01:09:31,438
That's the most one-dimensional.

1784
01:09:32,738 --> 01:09:34,668
It's blind criticism.

1785
01:09:34,668 --> 01:09:35,938
- "I knew you'd be like that." - Right.

1786
01:09:36,138 --> 01:09:37,608
"I knew you'd be like that."

1787
01:09:37,838 --> 01:09:39,438
- We got it. - Good!

1788
01:09:39,438 --> 01:09:41,178
It's going in! This one's going in!

1789
01:09:41,278 --> 01:09:42,478
- Tablo... - Shoot!

1790
01:09:42,608 --> 01:09:44,078
Shoot!

1791
01:09:44,518 --> 01:09:46,388
Someone should be waiting at the back!

1792
01:09:48,448 --> 01:09:50,358
- We got it! - Gosh, Mithra.

1793
01:09:50,358 --> 01:09:51,418
- Yellow card! - Red card.

1794
01:09:51,418 --> 01:09:53,228
- Is it okay to push like that? - How can he push Kang In...

1795
01:09:53,558 --> 01:09:55,458
- Doesn't that deserve a red card? - That's not right.

1796
01:09:55,458 --> 01:09:56,598
He pushed.

1797
01:09:56,598 --> 01:09:58,558
A death sentence for you.

1798
01:09:59,798 --> 01:10:00,898
A death sentence?

1799
01:10:01,698 --> 01:10:03,668
- A death sentence. - He can get ahead.

1800
01:10:04,238 --> 01:10:05,298
- A death sentence? - Yes.

1801
01:10:05,968 --> 01:10:07,938
- Sir, that's a bit... Yes. - No?

1802
01:10:08,938 --> 01:10:10,978
That's not exactly illegal.

1803
01:10:11,838 --> 01:10:12,978
The first-ever death sentence.

1804
01:10:12,978 --> 01:10:15,178
I think he deserves at least five years in prison.

1805
01:10:15,178 --> 01:10:17,618
(Lenient)

1806
01:10:17,618 --> 01:10:19,318
- A death sentence was too much. - Right?

1807
