01:19:29,328 --> 01:19:30,568
- It's legendary. - "They scored?"

2061
01:19:30,568 --> 01:19:31,738
He came out after cleaning himself up, right?

2062
01:19:32,568 --> 01:19:34,208
Why did you come out again? Stay in the bathroom.

2063
01:19:34,208 --> 01:19:36,338
It's not that. I'll go there when there's a crisis.

2064
01:19:36,338 --> 01:19:38,308
I can't stay in there forever.

2065
01:19:39,778 --> 01:19:41,448
You can't do that for the World Soccer Game?

2066
01:19:41,648 --> 01:19:44,378
If our team faces a crisis again,

2067
01:19:44,378 --> 01:19:45,448
- I'll go to the bathroom. - Okay.

2068
01:19:45,448 --> 01:19:47,518
Please go again if they don't score until the 40th minute.

2069
01:19:47,518 --> 01:19:49,218
- I'll go again. - No, the 37th minute.

2070
01:19:49,218 --> 01:19:50,758
I'll keep eating. Don't worry.

2071
01:19:50,758 --> 01:19:52,688
- I need to fuel up. - This is fun.

2072
01:19:52,918 --> 01:19:53,958
Let's go.

2073
01:19:54,658 --> 01:19:55,658
(The momentum has shifted already.)

2074
01:19:55,658 --> 01:19:57,858
From then on, Team Korea picked up the momentum.

2075
01:19:59,798 --> 01:20:00,798
Gosh, no.

2076
01:20:00,798 --> 01:20:02,028
(However...)

2077
01:20:02,628 --> 01:20:03,698
I knew that'd happen.

2078
01:20:03,698 --> 01:20:04,698
(They conceded from a set piece again.)

2079
01:20:04,698 --> 01:20:06,198
- That's when... - My heart dropped then.

2080
01:20:06,198 --> 01:20:07,968
- Back then... - Everyone went silent again then.

2081
01:20:08,808 --> 01:20:09,838
I knew that'd happen.

2082
01:20:13,908 --> 01:20:15,548
- It's offside! - It's offside!

2083
01:20:17,048 --> 01:20:18,178
(The goal was disallowed for offside.)

2084
01:20:18,178 --> 01:20:19,478
It's offside!

2085
01:20:19,618 --> 01:20:21,188
He totally went ahead.

2086
01:20:22,348 --> 01:20:23,658
- Hey. - Hey, look, you punk.

2087
01:20:23,658 --> 01:20:25,258
- You punk! - You brat.

2088
01:20:25,258 --> 01:20:26,288
- It's offside. - Hey!

2089
01:20:26,288 --> 01:20:28,558
- You little brat. - You're so impatient.

2090
01:20:28,558 --> 01:20:30,858
It was totally...

2091
01:20:30,858 --> 01:20:32,628
Gosh, I'm so glad.

2092
01:20:32,628 --> 01:20:33,668
(Relieved for real)

2093
01:20:33,768 --> 01:20:35,798
We change our stances so fast.

2094
01:20:35,868 --> 01:20:37,798
- Let's go. - Let's go!

2095
01:20:37,798 --> 01:20:38,868
(34th minute of 2nd half, Republic of Korea: 1, Czech Republic: 1)"

2096
01:20:38,868 --> 01:20:39,898
We have three minutes now.

2097
01:20:40,098 --> 01:20:41,908
Can you make the scoreboard with sand art?

2098
01:20:41,908 --> 01:20:42,908
Anything is possible with sand art.

2099
01:20:43,238 --> 01:20:45,178
- With sand art? - We can get all the details too.

2100
01:20:45,178 --> 01:20:46,178
- With sand art? - Yes.

2101
01:20:46,178 --> 01:20:48,678
Then to express the 34th minute, you should do this with sand.

2102
01:20:48,678 --> 01:20:51,748
- Like this. Anything is possible. - It's like a treasure hunt.

2103
01:20:51,748 --> 01:20:53,818
- Can you draw the audience too? - Of course. Anything is possible.

2104
01:20:53,818 --> 01:20:56,318
(34th minute of 2nd half, Republic of Korea: 1, Czech Republic: 1)

2105
01:20:57,418 --> 01:20:59,058
Time for Tablo to go to the bathroom.

2106
01:21:00,058 --> 01:21:01,258
It's the 34th minute.

2107
01:21:01,258 --> 01:21:03,488
You should go back in there if they don't score within three minutes.

2108
01:21:03,488 --> 01:21:05,398
- When should I go to the bathroom? - At the 37th minute.

2109
01:21:07,068 --> 01:21:08,668
- It's decided. - Darn it.

2110
01:21:08,798 --> 01:21:09,968
Don't watch the game on your phone in there.

2111
01:21:09,968 --> 01:21:10,968
My goodness.

2112
01:21:10,968 --> 01:21:12,198
You shouldn't be watching.

2113
01:21:12,198 --> 01:21:13,868
- Do something else. - I don't want to go again.

2114
01:21:13,868 --> 01:21:15,968
(Wait.)

2115
01:21:16,568 --> 01:21:18,478
- We got it. - We got it!

2116
01:21:18,938 --> 01:21:20,648
- We got it. - We got it!

2117
01:21:24,578 --> 01:21:27,688
- That's it. Oh Hyeon Gyu! - Oh Hyeon Gyu!

2118
01:21:27,948 --> 01:21:30,688
(Oh Hyeon Gyu's equalizer)

2119
01:21:30,888 --> 01:21:31,958
- We got it. - We got it!

2120
01:21:34,488 --> 01:21:35,888
(Shouting out the thrill of a comeback goal)

2121
01:21:35,888 --> 01:21:37,098
Gosh, he's crying.

2122
01:21:37,598 --> 01:21:39,098
- CODE KUNST! - He's crying.

2123
01:21:39,098 --> 01:21:40,968
Gosh, TACO KUNST.

2124
01:21:41,198 --> 01:21:42,598
I almost cried too, CODE KUNST.

2125
01:21:42,698 --> 01:21:44,038
I was really overwhelmed.

2126
01:21:44,038 --> 01:21:45,238
I almost cried too.

2127
01:21:45,238 --> 01:21:46,638
Everyone was overwhelmed by this.

2128
01:21:46,968 --> 01:21:48,608
It was my first time to cry while watching soccer.

2129
01:21:49,108 --> 01:21:51,238
- Really? - Being there made me cry.

2130
01:21:51,808 --> 01:21:53,538
It feels different at the stadium.

2131
01:21:53,538 --> 01:21:55,378
While I was cheering, a tear dropped.

2132
01:21:55,578 --> 01:21:56,908
It's the pride you have...

2133
01:21:56,908 --> 01:21:58,248
- for your country too. - That's right.

2134
01:21:58,518 --> 01:22:00,988
You'd feel more patriotic because you're in another country.

2135
01:22:02,818 --> 01:22:05,458
- Oh Hyeon Gyu. - Oh Hyeon Gyu!

2136
01:22:05,458 --> 01:22:07,128
- Oh Hyeon Gyu! I guessed right. - Oh Hyeon Gyu!

2137
01:22:07,258 --> 01:22:08,528
Gosh, Sir TACO KUNST.

2138
01:22:09,788 --> 01:22:11,528
I wish Oh Hyeon Gyu would score.

2139
01:22:11,528 --> 01:22:12,528
(CODE KUNST the Octopus is indeed amazing.)

2140
01:22:12,798 --> 01:22:14,768
(Dancing)

2141
01:22:17,438 --> 01:22:18,498
(Playing the saxophone with all his might...)

2142
01:22:18,498 --> 01:22:19,568
(to express how moved he is with the comeback goal)

2143
01:22:19,568 --> 01:22:21,768
You can't play that. Put it down.

2144
01:22:23,708 --> 01:22:25,038
That was perfect.

2145
01:22:25,238 --> 01:22:26,578
It's so funny.

2146
01:22:26,578 --> 01:22:28,278
- Be careful. - Hey!

2147
01:22:28,348 --> 01:22:29,378
No.

2148
01:22:30,478 --> 01:22:31,518
Kim Seung Gyu!

2149
01:22:31,518 --> 01:22:32,978
(Cheering)

2150
01:22:34,218 --> 01:22:35,388
- Kim Seung Gyu's save. - Kim Seung Gyu.

2151
01:22:35,388 --> 01:22:37,118
- Kim Seung Gyu. - It was amazing.

2152
01:22:37,118 --> 01:22:38,388
This one was incredible.

2153
01:22:38,388 --> 01:22:40,528
- How did he save it, really? - This one was dangerous.

2154
01:22:41,128 --> 01:22:43,088
- It went out. - We need to reward the goalkeeper.

2155
01:22:43,258 --> 01:22:45,058
We need to reward the goalkeeper?

2156
01:22:45,058 --> 01:22:46,128
- I haven't heard that in a while. - Gosh, Kim Seung Gyu.

2157
01:22:46,128 --> 01:22:47,398
- Seriously. - A prize.

2158
01:22:47,498 --> 01:22:49,128
Let's really give the goalkeeper an award.

2159
01:22:49,368 --> 01:22:50,968
- What a folksy expression. - That's folksy.

2160
01:22:50,968 --> 01:22:52,068
It's folksy.

2161
01:22:52,068 --> 01:22:53,068
(Rewarding him with clapping)

2162
01:22:53,068 --> 01:22:54,338
How did he save that, seriously?

2163
01:22:54,338 --> 01:22:55,568
That player is...

2164
01:22:55,568 --> 01:22:57,738
It's even more amazing than scoring.

2165
01:22:57,738 --> 01:22:58,908
Of course. Kim Seung Gyu...

2166
01:22:59,338 --> 01:23:00,848
They just need to hold out a little more.

2167
01:23:00,848 --> 01:23:02,678
Now that we're at it, let's score two more.

2168
01:23:02,678 --> 01:23:04,148
- Yes. Let's make it 4 to 1. - They need to keep pushing.

2169
01:23:04,378 --> 01:23:07,078
I can't believe they caught up like that all of a sudden.

2170
01:23:07,078 --> 01:23:08,118
I know.

2171
01:23:08,218 --> 01:23:10,418
(Right then, the Czech player appeals to the referee about pain.)

2172
01:23:10,418 --> 01:23:11,588
What's wrong with him?

2173
01:23:11,588 --> 01:23:13,118
Just bear with it! You're a professional athlete.

2174
01:23:14,558 --> 01:23:16,188
(He's reliable.)

2175
01:23:16,188 --> 01:23:18,158
You play soccer with your feet, not your face!

2176
01:23:19,098 --> 01:23:21,068
(Right then)

2177
01:23:21,068 --> 01:23:22,268
(The Czech team is threatening the goal again.)

2178
01:23:22,468 --> 01:23:24,838
That time. It was really hard.

2179
01:23:24,838 --> 01:23:26,168
- It's dangerous. - No!

2180
01:23:26,168 --> 01:23:27,768
(No!)

2181
01:23:27,768 --> 01:23:29,108
- No! - No.

2182
01:23:29,108 --> 01:23:30,478
(Brilliant Seung Gyu saves again.)

2183
01:23:30,478 --> 01:23:32,078
- Seung Gyu! - Brilliant Seung Gyu.

2184
01:23:32,078 --> 01:23:33,438
- Kim Seung Gyu is amazing. - Brilliant Seung Gyu.

2185
01:23:34,148 --> 01:23:35,278
- You should put on shades... - Gosh, Kim Seung Gyu.

2186
01:23:35,278 --> 01:23:36,378
- because he's too brilliant. - He is amazing.

2187
01:23:36,748 --> 01:23:37,778
- Yes. - Brilliant Seung Gyu.

2188
01:23:37,948 --> 01:23:39,048
(Relieved)

2189
01:23:39,048 --> 01:23:41,748
We need to give an award to the goalkeeper!

2190
01:23:41,748 --> 01:23:42,748
Applaud.

2191
01:23:42,748 --> 01:23:45,288
I've never seen CODE KUNST so immersed like this.

2192
01:23:45,288 --> 01:23:47,158
Does anyone know his address?

2193
01:23:47,588 --> 01:23:49,758
- I want to send him something. - He's the best.

2194
01:23:49,758 --> 01:23:51,298
- Kim Seung Gyu. - He's doing the work of ten.

2195
01:23:51,298 --> 01:23:55,298
I feel the most anxious in the last one minute and a half.

2196
01:23:55,768 --> 01:23:56,968
- Right. - It's the most nerve-racking.

2197
01:23:56,968 --> 01:23:58,238
- When you let your guard down, - That's right.

2198
01:23:58,238 --> 01:23:59,698
the goal goes in right away.

2199
01:23:59,698 --> 01:24:01,168
Do you know what I did at the stadium...

2200
01:24:01,168 --> 01:24:02,638
when only one minute was left?

2201
01:24:03,338 --> 01:24:04,538
I got up.

2202
01:24:04,538 --> 01:24:05,738
It's a heroic story.

2203
01:24:06,008 --> 01:24:08,608
"One minute!"

2204
01:24:08,608 --> 01:24:10,008
Every Mexican and Korean...

2205
01:24:10,008 --> 01:24:11,718
- "One minute!" - shouted, "One minute!"

2206
01:24:11,718 --> 01:24:12,918
- Even the Mexicans? - Saying there's one minute left.

2207
01:24:12,918 --> 01:24:14,688
- You led the cheer? - Yes, I did.

2208
01:24:14,688 --> 01:24:15,688
- That's... - Gosh.

2209
01:24:16,218 --> 01:24:17,988
I wanted to let the players know that there's one minute left.

2210
01:24:17,988 --> 01:24:19,118
"There's only one minute left!"

2211
01:24:19,118 --> 01:24:20,958
- I see. - "Hang in there until the end."

2212
01:24:20,958 --> 01:24:22,528
- You had such a deep intention? - Of course.

2213
01:24:22,528 --> 01:24:23,688
That's really nice.

2214
01:24:24,158 --> 01:24:25,698
- Darn. - No!

2215
01:24:26,058 --> 01:24:27,428
No. Go. Go get it.

2216
01:24:27,428 --> 01:24:28,428
- That's it! - No!

2217
01:24:28,428 --> 01:24:29,628
It's more nerve-racking because it's the last one.

2218
01:24:29,628 --> 01:24:31,338
- It's gut-wrenching. - Kick it hard!

2219
01:24:31,498 --> 01:24:33,098
- End it with a pass. - We got it.

2220
01:24:33,098 --> 01:24:35,308
- We got it. That's it. - Yes!

2221
01:24:35,308 --> 01:24:36,408
(The game ends. Korea wins with a score of 2 to 1.)

2222
01:24:36,568 --> 01:24:38,178
(Roaring)

2223
01:24:38,178 --> 01:24:39,938
- Gosh. - Goodness.

2224
01:24:39,938 --> 01:24:40,978
It was incredible.

2225
01:24:42,208 --> 01:24:44,078
For the 1st time in 16 years,

2226
01:24:44,518 --> 01:24:46,348
- we won the 1st game. - The 1st game.

2227
01:24:46,348 --> 01:24:47,348
Seriously.

2228
01:24:47,348 --> 01:24:48,518
How do we come together...

2229
01:24:48,518 --> 01:24:49,648
- as one with just one ball? - Tell me about it.

2230
01:24:49,648 --> 01:24:50,658
Seriously.

2231
01:24:50,658 --> 01:24:51,958
Do you know which song was played...

2232
01:24:51,958 --> 01:24:53,258
at the stadium after the game?

2233
01:24:53,258 --> 01:24:55,158
- Which song? - A DAY6's song.

2234
01:24:55,158 --> 01:24:56,928
- "Time of Our Life?" - That song was played.

2235
01:24:57,158 --> 01:24:59,328
- Really? - So everyone sang along.

2236
01:24:59,528 --> 01:25:00,698
They played it for Koreans.

2237
01:25:00,698 --> 01:25:02,368
Oh, it meant it was the time of our life.

2238
01:25:02,368 --> 01:25:05,168
(Precious time of our life)

2239
01:25:05,398 --> 01:25:06,438
They did so well.

2240
01:25:07,638 --> 01:25:10,708
I thought it was worth the four years' wait.

2241
01:25:10,808 --> 01:25:13,008
Team Korea always lost the game I got up to watch...

2242
01:25:13,008 --> 01:25:14,678
with sleepy eyes at home by myself.

2243
01:25:15,108 --> 01:25:16,948
I think we won because we watched it together.

2244
01:25:17,248 --> 01:25:19,418
Their faces turned redder...

2245
01:25:20,078 --> 01:25:21,688
than any kids' faces.

2246
01:25:21,688 --> 01:25:23,988
There was a moment when our faces were as red as the uniform.

2247
01:25:24,288 --> 01:25:26,218
I think it was fun because I watched it with the guys.

2248
01:25:26,358 --> 01:25:27,428
The game was at 11am,

2249
01:25:27,428 --> 01:25:30,228
so I thought it wouldn't be exciting.

2250
01:25:30,228 --> 01:25:31,658
But I think it was even better.

2251
01:25:31,658 --> 01:25:34,128
"I watched a soccer game..."

2252
01:25:34,128 --> 01:25:37,128
"and have the whole day to savor the joy of victory?"

2253
01:25:37,368 --> 01:25:38,838
I felt good the whole day.

2254
01:25:38,838 --> 01:25:40,398
Me too. Seriously.

2255
01:25:40,498 --> 01:25:42,838
I think soccer is the only thing...

2256
01:25:42,838 --> 01:25:45,008
that can make me break the calm.

2257
01:25:45,378 --> 01:25:46,878
- You look the happiest. - Seriously.

2258
01:25:47,308 --> 01:25:49,348
My voice went hoarse for the first time in my life...

2259
01:25:49,348 --> 01:25:50,678
because of soccer.

2260
01:25:51,178 --> 01:25:52,918
It could've been my first time...

2261
01:25:53,048 --> 01:25:55,018
having fried chicken in the morning.

2262
01:25:55,018 --> 01:25:56,948
I think today will be memorable.

2263
01:25:58,488 --> 01:25:59,588
We're leaving.

2264
01:26:00,058 --> 01:26:01,088
Take this.

2265
01:26:01,088 --> 01:26:02,528
They left right away?

2266
01:26:02,788 --> 01:26:04,928
- You didn't have a party afterward? - They're leaving right away?

2267
01:26:05,098 --> 01:26:06,958
They went back to their daily life...

2268
01:26:06,958 --> 01:26:08,428
to pick up their kids from kindergarten.

2269
01:26:08,668 --> 01:26:09,898
I'm worried.

2270
01:26:10,228 --> 01:26:11,398
I'm worried CODE KUNST would ask us to watch a soccer game together...

2271
01:26:11,398 --> 01:26:12,538
whenever there is one.

2272
01:26:12,868 --> 01:26:14,808
That's what made me feel so good.

2273
01:26:14,808 --> 01:26:17,378
Because the team won, we promised to watch the next one together.

2274
01:26:17,378 --> 01:26:18,378
- Of course. - That's right.

2275
01:26:18,378 --> 01:26:19,578
Let's watch together again next time.

2276
01:26:19,638 --> 01:26:20,948
- Come to our office. - Come to our office.

2277
01:26:20,948 --> 01:26:21,978
We're leaving.

2278
01:26:22,578 --> 01:26:24,448
- Bye, guys. - See you.

2279
01:26:24,748 --> 01:26:26,248
(Next story)

2280
01:26:26,478 --> 01:26:29,148
(Feeling stiff)

2281
01:26:29,148 --> 01:26:30,988
(It's already noon?)

2282
01:26:31,618 --> 01:26:33,818
(Today is a day off.)

2283
01:26:33,988 --> 01:26:35,288
(I think I'm having a day off after 3 weeks.)

2284
01:26:35,528 --> 01:26:39,598
(A perfect day to catch up on the house chores she put off)

2285
01:26:40,058 --> 01:26:42,298
(Turning on the air conditioner before doing the chores)

2286
01:26:44,868 --> 01:26:46,898
(The lowest temperature shouldn't be 29°C.)

2287
01:26:47,198 --> 01:26:49,168
(The air conditioner is causing trouble from the start.)

2288
01:26:49,408 --> 01:26:51,008
(Still, let's start cleaning the windows...)

2289
01:26:51,008 --> 01:26:52,638
(for a change of mood.)

2290
01:26:52,938 --> 01:26:54,948
(Squeaking)

2291
01:26:55,048 --> 01:26:56,608
(The posture is making her hotter when it's already hot.)

2292
01:26:56,608 --> 01:26:57,718
(Squeaking)

2293
01:26:57,718 --> 01:27:00,048
(Is this a penalty or what?)

2294
01:27:00,278 --> 01:27:03,148
(Today is a mess.)

2295
01:27:04,018 --> 01:27:06,218
(But today's the only day off.)

2296
01:27:06,688 --> 01:27:09,558
(Let's make a proper meal for myself since I worked hard.)

2297
01:27:10,798 --> 01:27:11,898
(Savoring)

2298
01:27:11,958 --> 01:27:13,958
(Yes, this is it.)

2299
01:27:14,568 --> 01:27:18,468
(Let's relieve it with a bite.)

2300
01:27:18,838 --> 01:27:20,708
(Whether it's food or happiness, I'm the one to make it.)

2301
01:27:20,708 --> 01:27:21,968
(Taking a bite)

2302
01:27:22,808 --> 01:27:24,078
(Grabbing)

2303
01:27:24,478 --> 01:27:26,808
(I feel the happiest now.)

2304
01:27:27,178 --> 01:27:28,578
(Lucky Day)

2305
01:27:28,578 --> 01:27:30,508
(Big Appetite Day)

2306
01:27:34,388 --> 01:27:37,518
(Someone is visiting Ji Hyeon.)

2307
01:27:38,388 --> 01:27:40,258
(The first Rainbow Club member to visit Ji Hyeon's place,)

2308
01:27:40,258 --> 01:27:41,328
(CODE KUNST)

2309
01:27:41,588 --> 01:27:43,928
(People always tell me that I don't dress well.)

